window.MONARCH_CHAPTERS=(window.MONARCH_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":51,"title":"Chapter 51: End Of the First Incident (2)","paragraphs":["Damien, despite not being able to use mana and having strain on his body, still moved.","He was slowly getting better at moving his body after resting for a while. So fighting physically without any mana was possible for him.","CLANG!","The man in front of him was really strong, but not so strong that he couldn’t be killed.","The problem was that the man was so experienced and skilled at fighting that landing a fatal hit on him was nearly impossible.","Whether they attacked at the same time or tried another plan to attack him, Petrick always dodged or blocked all attacks that were harmful to him.","Now, after what Noah said about him using his lifespan, Petrick’s overall strength had increased.","As Noah had told Damien, he told Regnar in short what to do while fighting.","Regnar’s condition was very bad. A slash on his front, cuts all over his body. He had taken a lot of damage but avoided most of the life-taking strikes.","While Draven was still standing tall despite being injured so much. His will to fight only intensified further as he fought someone stronger than himself. That’s how Barbarians actually were. They did not give up until the end.","Now, with the involvement of Arisha and Damien, it became harder once again for Petrick to kill Draven and Regnar.","Damien’s blade clashed against Petrick’s dagger coated with black smoky darkness.","Damien’s muscles bulged at the strong force he was feeling from Petrick’s attack.","A kick landed on Damien’s already weak body.","\"Gahh!!\" He was thrown back and rolled on the ground.","Three arrows made up of water, thin and sharp, shot toward Petrick.","He sidestepped, ducked, and slashed the last one.","Draven, with a bloodied face, moved closer to him with full rage.","\"Arreghh!\" He screamed like giving a battle cry. His face had several cuts, cheeks bruised. Blood was dripping from his mouth.","Despite all of this, the courage to fight never went down.","Yet Petrick beat the three of them badly.","Damien, Draven, and Regnar were all injured more and more as the fight continued.","Petrick’s dagger slashed at Draven’s shoulder, at Damien’s knee, and a kick landed on Regnar’s chest where a diagonal cut was formed.","Despite that, no one died.","Because Arisha saved them from a distance each time Petrick tried to attack with a strike that might kill someone. She supported them and covered them again and again.","Her breathing was ragged. Her fingers were slightly bleeding from using the bow. More than anything, her mana was near its limit.","Petrick tried to attack Damien at his neck.","Airsha pulled the string of her bow, a pure blue color arrow form immediately. It trembled. Still she released it as the arrow shot towards Petrick’s arm.","Which made him turned his dagger trajectory towards the arrow. Because of that Damien stepped away from him.","But that was last. Finally Arisha dropped on one knee exhausted. She was hoping this battle would end quickly.","While others were fighting, Noah got near them and then waved at Damien, giving him a signal that it was time.","Damien nodded in understanding. He moved faster with his injured body. Pain shot through all over, yet he moved.","Petrick had just clashed an attack with Draven when Damien moved and took the chance. He then yelled at Regnar, who was on his left side.","\"Now!\"","When Damien said that, Regnar extended both his hands, letting his hammer fall on the road. He conjured two magic spells at the same time. Grey magic circles appeared in front of his arms.","From Regnar’s left side came Noah. He had taken his spear again in his right hand. His left hand extended as he started to channel mana to conjure a magic spell that he had never used before. The spell was snow mist.","Damien closed in and took the chance to grab one of Petrick’s arms from the shoulder. The strength in Petrick was too much to hold him properly for Damien.","\"Argh! What are you doing, boy!\" Petrick asked with his dark eyes glaring at him dangerously.","When Petrick tried to move his right hand to kill Damien with his dagger, at that time Draven held him in the same way, letting his battle axe fall.","\"Not so fast!\" Draven said.","While Regnar’s spells were conjured. He was just a few meters away from the three. The spells were Sound Burst,","[Sound Burst]","As loud sound waves burst from the magic circles toward Petrick’s face, and he was hit by them.","Everything happened too fast. Just a few seconds ago Petrick was held by the other two.","Just then the spell was launched at him.","Both attacks hit Petrick on his face perfectly.","Petrick’s head was thrown back by the impact of the sound wave.","\"ARRGGHHHH!!!\" Petrick screamed.","His ears were ringing and he could not hear anything for a while. His brain throbbed, not understanding what was happening around him.","Yet he still held his dagger firmly in both hands, not letting them fall down.","Just like him, Draven and Damien were hit slightly by the attack. Both of them left Petrick’s body and got away while covering their ears.","Arisha wanted to shoot an arrow at him while he was defenseless.","But she was at her limit.","They also felt similar to Petrick, but not as much as him.","At that moment, Noah forced himself to form the spell.","’Damn! I thought she might attack him... and kill him... but I guess she’s at her limit... now I have to try this idiotic plan of mine.’ He thought with annoyance.","Mana began flowing through his mana veins, moving from his core, through his arm, and into his palm. He could feel the cold energy gathering at his fingertips as he tried to control the flow.","In front of his hand, thin snow-blue lines began to appear in the air, forming the structure of a magic circle he had memorized long ago. The lines connected one by one, forming symbols, runic patterns, and mana pathways.","But the moment the circle began to stabilize, it started trembling.","The lines flickered. Then the patterns inside flickered. The mana pathways became uneven.","The circle was unstable.","Noah immediately understood the problem. The mana input was inconsistent, the flow speed was wrong, and some pathways were receiving too much mana while others were receiving too little.","In a normal situation, a mage would stop the spell immediately.","But Noah didn’t. He just couldn’t.","’I am not giving up here.’ His eyes filled with determination.","He gritted his teeth and forced more mana into the circle.","’I cannot stop now... I want to use it no matter what!’ He encouraged himself.","The snow-blue circle brightened violently as more mana was pushed into it. The unstable pathways began to crack, glowing brighter and brighter as the structure failed to handle the pressure. It shook uncontrollably.","\"Form... already!\" he shouted."]},{"number":52,"title":"Chapter 52: End Of the First Incident (3)","paragraphs":["The snow-blue circle brightened violently as more mana was pushed into it. The unstable pathways began to crack, glowing brighter and brighter as the structure failed to handle the pressure. It shook uncontrollably.","\"Form... already!\" he shouted.","His brain throbbed painfully. Despite that, he didn’t stop there.","At the same time, he focused on Petrick, mostly on the road beneath him.","Some mana traveled through his legs towards Petrick, then formed a small patch of ice beneath him. This was much easier for him compared to conjuring a new spell. It was done faster.","While the structure was still hard to maintain, it was wrong from the beginning.","The magic circle was formed, but it was wrong.","So, the mana flow collided inside the circle. The patterns broke. The pathways shattered. And the magic circle collapsed.","But Noah didn’t stop providing his mana.","CRACK!","The circle exploded in a burst of mana.","The backlash traveled directly into Noah’s hand. The mana veins in his left arm twisted violently, and a sharp cracking sound echoed as tiny fractures formed in his bones and veins.","Blood burst out from his palm and fingers, streaming down his arm.","Usually, someone would not take this much damage. But because Noah had provided excessive mana to it, he received a strong backlash.","But despite the explosion...","The spell still partially activated.","From the shattered magic circle, a massive amount of snow mist burst out like a broken dam releasing water.","Cold air spread rapidly.","White mist flooded the battlefield.","Within seconds, the snow mist became so dense that it covered several meters in every direction, turning the entire area into a white fog where nothing could be seen.","No one knew what was inside the mist.","Only the cold, silent snow mist filled the battlefield.","But Noah... he could sense something inside the snow mist much better. Was it because he was the one who made the snow mist?","Or maybe because of his affinity towards ice.","Noah’s left hand was injured, yet he moved inside the fog with the spear held tightly in his right hand.","He moved in the same direction where Petrick was standing.","Inside the mist,","Petrick remained standing where he was, covering his ears, trying to get back to his senses.","He couldn’t understand what was going on. The mist spread everywhere, making his vision useless. The sound attack was still ringing in his ears. His brain throbbed painfully. Just then something moved beneath his feet.","The small ice that had formed beneath him started to increase out of nowhere, freezing his legs and locking them in place.","\"What the?\" Petrick was confused, trying to break free from them.","At the same time, a sword shot at him from the left side.","Petrick couldn’t sense it at all. Where did it come from?","The sword struck his upper arm.","Crushed.","Splashed.","Blood splattered on the ground from the sword strike.","\"ARGGHHH!!!\"","Just then someone moved behind him.","He was slightly better in his senses now.","But too late to react. Not forgetting his legs being frozen, which already had a few cracks, but an attack came to him faster than anything.","Behind him, Noah came with his spear, his eyes filled with determination and resolve to kill his enemy.","His one hand was injured, blood dripping from it.","His body had injuries and wounds all over.","The spear he held in his right hand moved with intense speed and strength.","Schlick","The tip of the spear blade tore through the nape of Petrick’s neck as it came out from the front side of his throat.","Splattered.","Blood gushed out like a fountain.","\"Gah‐!\" Petrick groaned. He wanted to scream loudly in pain, yet he couldn’t since his throat was destroyed.","They remained in the same position for a while.","\"Hah.... haf... hah..\" Noah breathed raggedly.","Petrick was nearly dead.","But suddenly he turned his head 180 degrees.","Facing Noah’s face.","Noah’s eyes went wide in horror.","His black void like eyes started at Noah’s blue eyes. There was a wide smile on Petrick’s face. Despite the torn throat, he somehow muttered, \"I-I-I w-will kill you nex-\"","But Noah didn’t let him finish.","He spun the spear in his hand and swung his spear to the other side violently.","More than half of his head was cut from the neck. But it couldn’t take the weight of the whole head, so it finally fell on the ground.","Thud.","The blood came out from the neck like a fountain, falling over Noah, which drenched his face with blood.","Then Petrick’s body fell on the ground with a loud thud.","Noah gazed at the dead face of Petrick. The creepy smile on his face didn’t go away.","Finally, the battle was over. Killing him felt easier this way.","The mist slowly started to subside in the air.","---","Some distance away from where Noah and the others were fighting Petrick,","Monsters were still destroying things.","Lyria and Leonard, who were fighting those monsters, were trying to stop them from going in the direction where the others were.","They were also tired.","But just then a cracking sound came from above the sky.","Both looked up at the sky, only to see something breaking apart. It was like transparent glass in the sky above them was breaking.","Shattered.","Soon it shattered into thin particles, vanishing into nothingness.","Just then the monsters who were rampaging suddenly stopped.","Lyria and Leonard now observed those monsters.","Their bodies went rigid, not moving even an inch.","And the next moment, all of their bodies burst into blood by an unknown force.","\"What’s happening?\" Leonard wondered.","\"How are they dead?!\" While Lyria Said with shocked expression.","Then they felt as if someone was watching them from above.","They raised their heads to look at who it was.","There in the sky was the floating form of an old man with white hair and black eyes. He wore a black suit.","\"P-Principal.\"","He was Adrian Aegeus.","His black eyes roamed over the whole area.","He killed all the monsters in that place without even touching them. That was the strength of a person who was at the peak level of human ranks."]},{"number":53,"title":"Chapter 53: End of The First Incident (4)","paragraphs":["The moment Noah beheaded Petrick’s body.","Somewhere away from Novaris Academy.","In the same Novaris city, inside a room of a small hotel, lay a man on a single bed. The curtains of the room were closed and the lights were off.","The man lay motionless.","His fingers twitched. His eyelids shook as he slowly opened his eyes. His black eyes stared at the ceiling lazily.","The man pushed himself upright. His dark brown hair was messy. Sweat dripped from his forehead slowly. The man looked around; he was in his late thirties.","His right hand moved to his neck, slowly running over it. \"I could still feel that pain on my neck.\"","He put his legs on the floor while sitting at the edge of the bed and stretched his body. \"Damien... that boy was really something else. I need to inform about this to Malv— I mean boss... I should give respect to that old man. hehe~\" He chuckled, then muttered.","\"Damien is really dangerous talent. Able to kill a peak D rank monster by himself... and that monster was not normal. It was strong enough to kill Rank C monsters. I specially caught him for them.\" He talked to himself with a small smile.","\"...and that boy with white hair... who was he? I didn’t ask his name. Haha! He was interesting. I have to kill him in future.\"","\"For now, let’s inform Boss.\"","The man took out his mobile, then called a private number.","Soon it was picked up from the other side.","---","The battle was over.","The mist had subsided in the air.","Some distance away, Arisha sat on the ground without caring about anything. After all, they finally killed him.","While Regnar leaned against the broken building, wounds all over his body, he still had a satisfied face.","Draven lay on the road while looking up at the sky motionlessly. He muttered in a low voice, \"Good job... Noah.\" He was not in better condition either. Wounds all over his body. Cuts on his hands and a big wound on his knees. Blood was still streaming down from them onto the ground.","Just away from him sat Damien. His sword fell on the road. Both hands were behind him on either side to support his body from not falling onto the road.","Noah, meanwhile, remained standing near the dead body, still standing with the support of his spear. Blood dripped from his hand and cuts all over his body.","Finally, he was able to kill Petrick.","\"I-I kill....\" He blinked dazedly. In the matter of survival, he didn’t even think that it was his first kill. That he had never killed anyone before. Not just him, but even the old Noah had never killed any human before.","The thought that he was going to kill someone never entered his mind. If that was not enough, the way he killed Petrick was kind of brutal in his eyes. The blood was splattered around like a fountain, painting the surroundings.","His heart started to beat faster. His breathing became ragged. His vision was getting blurry.","He couldn’t tell why he was feeling like this. Was it because the realization that he killed someone came to him? Or was it because he lost so much blood and was exhausted?","He knew that the man was controlling the body of a worker named Petrick. What if Petrick was alive and innocent in this? The man behind all of this was not dead, but Petrick was dead. By the hands of Noah.","Noah gazed at the head of Petrick, which still had a smile on his face.","Soon a smile broke on Noah’s face. ’It doesn’t matter... I survived..’ The smile came because he was still able to beat that man. Land a last hit on him. Even though he was using someone else’s body, he was feeling pain each time he got hit by a strong strike.","So Noah felt nice about that. About landing the last hit on him. He shook his head and tried to push unnecessary thoughts away.","\"You okay, Noah?\" Damien asked from his side with a smile. \"You did a good job, man.\"","Noah smiled at him while nodding. \"Yeah... I guess I did... no... We did a good job.\" He closed his eyes for a second. He was on verge of loosing consciousness. He kepy them closer for a while, then opened them only to find himself in another place.","\"What the hell? Where am I?\" he muttered in a low voice.","Noah looked around to see what was there.","Everywhere was empty space. There was no ground and no light.","Darkness stretched in every direction. It felt like he was floating, yet he could feel something beneath his feet. Or maybe he couldn’t. He wasn’t sure.","The silence was terrifying.","There was no wind. He couldn’t hear anything or see anything. Just darkness.","A strange fear crawled over his body like cold insects moving under his skin. His heartbeat started to increase.","Thump.","Thump.","Thump.","The sound of his own heartbeat echoed in that empty darkness, making him even more uneasy.","\"W-Where is this place...?\" he whispered again, but even his voice sounded strange, as if the darkness swallowed the sound before it could travel.","He started walking slowly, looking around carefully, but no matter how much he walked, nothing changed. The darkness remained the same in every direction.","His heartbeat became faster.","Thump-thump.","Thump-thump.","Thump-thump.","Then suddenly a huge wave of hot wind slammed into his face.","WHOOSH!","Noah stumbled back a step, raising his arm to cover his face. The wind was hot, like air coming from a furnace, and it carried a strange metallic smell.","It smelled like blood.","Noah slowly lowered his arm and looked toward the direction from where the hot wind had come.","At first, he saw nothing.","But then two enormous blood-red eyes opened in the darkness.","They were gigantic, far larger than any creature’s eyes should be. Each eye was like a giant crimson moon floating in the void. Black vertical slit pupils stared directly at Noah.","The moment Noah’s eyes met those red eyes, a terrifying pressure fell on him. His body froze instantly. He couldn’t move nor could he breathe.","Then pain came. Intense, unbearable pain shot through his entire body as if millions of needles were piercing him from inside.","\"AAAAHHHHHHHHH!!!\" Noah screamed loudly in pain, his eyes wide open.","It felt like his bones were being crushed, his veins were being torn apart, and his organs were being squeezed by invisible hands.","Blood started streaming down from his eyes, then from his nose, then from his mouth.","His vision started shaking violently, but those red eyes remained clear in front of him, staring at him without blinking.","The pressure increased.","Tiny cracks began appearing on Noah’s skin, like glass about to shatter. From them blood started to leak.","\"AAAAAAAHHHHH!!!\" he screamed again, his voice breaking.","His arms started breaking apart as blood splattered from them. Then his chest. And then his legs.","His entire body began to shatter.","The cracks spread everywhere across his body. He tried to move. Tried to scream. Tried to look away from those eyes. But he just couldn’t move.","The red eyes kept staring at him.","They were cold, ancient, and terrifying.","His body completely shattered into small pieces of flesh."]},{"number":54,"title":"Chapter 54: Finally Safe","paragraphs":["\"AAAAAAA!!\" A loud scream echoed inside the big room.","Noah sat upright on the bed, his eyes wide open in shock, fear, and a sense of danger.","\"Haf... haff... haf...\" He gasped for breath as his breathing was ragged. Sweat dripped down his whole body, drenching his clothes. His blue eyes, filled with horror, stared ahead.","Gulp.","He swallowed hard as his hands instantly ran over his body. He checked his muscles, his arms, his chest, and then ran his hands over his neck and whole face.","There were no cracks on his body, just a few bandages here and there.","Only then did he notice his surroundings and feel slightly relieved.","\"What the hell happened, Noah?! Why did you scream suddenly?\" Regnar asked from beside him in a worried voice, his brows furrowed. It was a familiar voice.","Noah turned and saw Regnar lying on a white bed beside him.","His arms had bandages. The bruises and cuts on his face had been healed.","\"Yeah... you okay?\" Damien asked from the other side of Noah, looking at him with concern.","On the other side of Noah was another bed, and on that bed was Damien.","\"Oh... I...\" Noah hesitated.","The memory of finding himself in that unknown place and seeing those two moon-like eyes of an unknown entity flashed in his mind. The pain he felt after looking into those eyes was something he had never experienced before. His whole body had shattered into pieces.","’Was that my dream?’ he thought while still trying to calm himself down.","’It was so real... I can’t believe it was just a dream.’","\"Hey, Noah... are you okay?\" Damien asked once more, his expression slightly serious.","Pulling Noah out of his thoughts, he replied, \"Hm... yes... I am okay... just had a nightmare...\"","\"Student Noah, what happened?\"","Just then, a woman in a white lab coat came towards him. She had black hair and was in charge of the infirmary.","\"Oh... I am fine... I just had a bad nightmare.\" Noah replied.","She observed his complexion—how his body was covered with sweat, his breathing, and his facial expression.","She walked closer to him, then took a soft, clean cloth that was neatly folded and kept on the small table beside Noah’s bed. She started to clean the sweat from his face.","\"It seems you really had a bad dream. Well, calm down now... you are no longer in danger,\" she said gently as she softly wiped his sweat.","Noah didn’t stop her. Finally, his heartbeat started to slow down. He understood that he was in the infirmary and that they were safe now.","The room was huge, with many beds arranged in rows on both sides. Many students were sleeping on them, injured. A few of them were awake, probably because of Noah’s loud yelling.","Soft, dim lights were on at the corners of the room, giving enough light to see while still being dim enough for others to sleep without problems.","His eyes traveled to the clock on the wall.","’It’s 9 o’clock at night.’","The woman wiped his face, then stepped away from him.","\"You should rest now. You will be fine by tomorrow,\" she said calmly.","\"Thank you,\" Noah replied simply.","She gave him a small smile and left.","He lay back on the bed.","\"So... will you tell us what dream you saw?\" Regnar asked from his bed curiously, tilting his head slightly.","\"It was nothing... just saw myself dying... and woke up...\" He gave him half answer.","’It was a dream... that lasted less than one minute... yet it felt like hours had passed.’ He thought about how he saw dream for around a minute...but he was unconscious for hours.","\"That’s one bad dream you saw,\" Damien commented, exhaling lightly.","\"By the way... what actually happened? I don’t remember... when I fell unconscious,\" Noah asked.","\"Hm... you were fine... no, not fine. You were pretty injured and had lost too much blood, yet you were still standing there with the support of your spear. When I said good job... you smiled... then fell forward onto the ground unconscious,\" Damien explained calmly.","\"Is that so... well, it’s good that we are safe.\"","\"Yeah... the moment you killed that bastard, the barrier broke like glass. And the next moment, the principal came and killed all the monsters in seconds,\" Regnar said with a slight grin.","\"Ohh nice~\" Noah commented.","’The fuck? If the principal was here... shouldn’t he be strong enough to break the barrier and enter... or shouldn’t that powerhouse have the strength to teleport inside it?’","Noah didn’t know much about Adrian. But he did know that Adrian was considered one of the strongest beings in this world.","’Hmm... then it must be well planned... the one who created that barrier should be someone as strong as Adrian... or maybe stronger than him.’","Noah tried to make some speculations.","\"You are in deep thought again?\" Damien said lazily, putting both hands behind his head while staring up at the ceiling.","\"I was just thinking about that incident again... well, let’s put that aside... you two seem okay now... where are the others?\"","\"Look beside me...\" Damien said, turning his head to the other side.","On his other side, Leonard was sleeping.","\"Wait? He’s here?... is he asleep?\" Noah asked in slight surprise.","\"I was... but woke up because of you,\" Leonard replied calmly while facing the other side, lying sideways.","\"Sorry about that...\" Noah said apologetically.","Then he turned to the right side where Regnar was, and on his other side was Draven, who was in deep slumber.","\"That guy didn’t wake up even after I screamed...\"","\"Yeah... he’s sure in deep sleep,\" Regnar chuckled while looking at Draven.","\"By the way... where is Arisha? Is she okay?\" Noah asked, wondering about her and Lyria.","\"You already missing me? Well, I am alright. Don’t worry about me,\" came a calm reply from the beds across them. Her voice was sharp and clear. On the other side, Arisha was lying down. More like resting.","Noah raised his head slightly to look at her.","\"I did miss you... hehe,\" he laughed softly. \"Thanks for helping me back then...\" He put his head back against the cushion.","\"No need to thank me. We all just did what was right at that time...\" Arisha replied in her usual cool and indifferent tone.","\"Okay. Where is Lyria?\"","\"I am just beside Arisha,\" came a gentle voice.","\"How are you? You okay?\" Noah asked.","\"Yes, I am... what about you, Noah? Are you okay now?\" she asked gently.","\"I am better. Thanks for asking.\"","’She’s kind and sweet, like always.’","Noah then pushed himself up, trying to get out of bed.","\"Where are you going, Noah?\" Regnar asked, raising a brow.","\"Washroom. Where is it?\"","Regnar pointed to the left side.","Noah got up from the bed. His body still ached in pain, but walking was possible.","He walked towards the washroom."]},{"number":55,"title":"Chapter 55: Sweet Reward","paragraphs":["Noah slowly walked towards the washroom, holding his side slightly because his body still ached from the injuries. Each step reminded him of the battle, the wounds, the exhaustion, and the blood he had lost.","He pushed the washroom door open and entered.","The bright white light inside made him squint his eyes for a moment. The room was quiet and clean. White tiles covered the walls and floor. A long mirror was fixed above the basins, and the faint smell of disinfectant filled the air.","He walked to one of the urinals and relieved himself. After finishing, he moved towards the basin and turned on the tap.","Cold water flowed out.","He splashed water on his face once.","Then again. Then did it again.","He kept washing his face many times with cold water, as if trying to wash away something more than just sweat and dirt.","Finally, he stopped and sighed deeply. He slowly looked up at the mirror. His face stared back at him.","His face was still handsome as ever, though there were a few small bandages here and there. His blue eyes looked slightly tired, but they were still sharp.","But he was still not fully calm.","It was not the incident or killing another person that shook him.","It was the memory of that dream.","Every time he thought about those eyes, fear crawled over his body unknowingly. His heart would start beating faster, and a strange cold feeling would spread through his chest.","He placed both hands on the basin and lowered his head for a moment.","\"Calm down... it was just a dream...\" he muttered to himself.","But even he didn’t believe that completely. Then he slowly raised his head again.","There was another reason why he came here. He looked at the blue translucent screen floating in front of him.","It was written on it.","[If you are awake, click Yes]","There was only a Yes option.","Earlier, he was so afraid and confused that he didn’t even think much about it. But now he was alone here, and the lights were bright.","He stared at the screen for a few seconds. Then he raised his hand and touched Yes. The moment he touched it, the screen flickered slightly.","Then the same kind of text he had seen in the hospital appeared in front of him.","After touching Yes, another text appeared.","[Congratulations, Noah Eldritch, an extra has survived the first Act of Chapter 1: The Puppet]","[For surviving this incident and even contributing and killing the main villain of this act, you will be getting a Five-Star Manual for Weapon Art. It is an ancient sword art related to ice affinity users]","A martial manual was like a legacy left behind by a strong ancient figure. Everything they learned or created about that art, condensed into writing so the next generation can inherit their art style.","Finding one is like finding a dead legend’s entire lifetime of knowledge sitting in your hands.","Manuals...or more like martial manuals were separated into five grades, From one start to five star.","There were many manuals which are created by heroes or adventures of this times as well. Though most of them were from one star to three star.","So Noah’s eyes widened slightly as he read everything.","Then he read further.","[While since you did not just survive but killed the main villain, you will be getting a bonus reward. As an ice creation ability user who can create anything and use different weapons during a fight, you are bestowed with a new profession. You won’t be seeing your other professions on your status window anymore.]","[Combatant - Level 1]","Soon he felt a slight pain all over his body, but just for a second. It felt like light lightning roaming over his body. His muscles twitched slightly, and he felt something change inside his body.","An information came to inside him.","’A person who specializes in combat and multiple weapons.’","Then suddenly, an ice-blue colored book appeared in midair in front of him.","Noah instinctively caught it. The screen showed one last line.","[Enjoy your reward. Bye Extra. See you next time if you survive]","Then the screen disappeared.","Noah blinked.","Everything had happened too fast. He looked at the thin book in his hand. It was very thin and cold to the touch, almost like it was made of ice.","He opened the book, which was sword art manual. Inside, the pages were black.","Only a few words were written on the first page.","Frozen Lotus Blade Art","Under that, it was written.","To learn this, just put mana inside it.","Noah stared at the book for a moment.","’That’s...easy..’ He did as it was written.","He slowly poured a small amount of mana into the book.","The moment he did that, the book began to glow in a soft light blue hue.","Then suddenly the book turned into tiny particles of blue light and flew straight into Noah’s forehead.","\"Agh—!\"","A sharp pain shot through his head. He immediately fell on his rear on the washroom floor.","Thud.","And then grabbed his head tightly.","The pain was intense, like someone was forcing huge amounts of information into his brain.","\"Gah-!\" He was going to scream again. But stopped as he bit his forearm tightly so his scream wouldn’t come out.","His teeth sank into his skin, and blood started coming out, but he didn’t care.","After a few minutes of sharp pain, it slowly started to subside.","Breathing heavily, he slowly released his forearm. Blood streamed from the bite mark.","He gasped for air while rubbing his head.","Unknown knowledge of the sword art was now inside his brain. Movements, stances, techniques, mana flow, sword paths, everything appeared in his mind like memories that were always there.","He cursed under his breath, \"This damn thing...\"","But then a small smile appeared on his face as he tried to understand the sword art.","Slowly, that small smile turned wider.","His face looked almost crazy as he realized how strong this sword art was. It was extremely powerful and clearly a very high-rank sword art.","Then he also received information about his Combatant profession. The more he understood it, the wider his smile became.","And then Nah started laughing loudly inside the washroom.","\"HAHAHAHAHA!\"","He was very happy for getting those rewards. That he forgot about that dream altogether.","---","Outside the washroom, in the infirmary, Damien, Regnar, Arisha, and Lyria all looked towards the washroom direction after hearing faint laughter.","Damien slowly raised an eyebrow. Regnar frowned slightly. Lyria looked confused.","Arisha blinked once, then said in a calm voice, \"Is he gone mad? Oh my... I hope God could help him.\""]},{"number":56,"title":"Chapter 56: Weight Of Responsibility (1)","paragraphs":["It was nighttime, yet Adrian came back to his office.","He slumped down in his chair after a long day.","They had gone through something terrible that the academy had never faced in so many years. A single person had entered and killed so many students, yet they couldn’t do anything.","Now he had to answer to the parents who had lost their children. They had believed in the academy as a place that could make them stronger, better. Not to kill them.","Adrian rubbed his temples, his expression heavy and tired.","\"Malrick...\" he muttered, his eyes narrowing slightly as the name left his lips.","Just then, he noticed a black metallic device on the table. It was small, something that could be held in his palm easily.","Adrian’s gaze sharpened instantly.","His tired expression disappeared, replaced by cold alertness.","He slowly leaned forward, narrowing his eyes further, already guessing who had placed it there.","\"Is this... put here by the same man who attacked inside the academy... or is there another person... who works for Malrick while staying here at the academy?...I need to check cameras..but probably it won’t have anything. They won’t make such normal mistake.\" Adrian muttered under his breath, suspicion flickering across his face.","He extended his hand and touched the flat surface of the device. The moment his fingers made contact.","The device suddenly lit up. A blue light emerged from its surface, illuminating Adrian’s face with a cold glow.","His eyes reflected that light as his expression turned serious. A screen formed in the air, and a video started playing on it.","In the video sat a man behind a desk. The moment Adrian saw him. His eyes narrowed further. A faint tension appeared in his jaw.","He was of a similar age to Adrian. Long white hair with some grey streaks was tied in a ponytail, indicating age. His violet eyes were sharp and indifferent, and a white beard covered his lower face.","Adrian’s fingers slowly curled into a fist on the armrest.","\"If you are watching this video, that means the incident has already occurred in the academy. It must have been successful. How did you like my gift, Adrian... my old friend?\"","The man’s heavy voice came out from the video.","Adrian’s gaze turned colder. Even though it was just a recording, the weight behind those words was undeniable.","A faint muscle in Adrian’s cheek twitched, but he remained silent.","\"Now you must be wondering why I did this? Well, you already know the answer. Didn’t I say to you years ago... I won’t ever forgive you... and now it’s time for me to make my moves. Firstly, I attacked the academy you took care of for so many years as Principal.\"","The man smirked mockingly. At that moment, Adrian’s eyes hardened.","His fingers tightened slightly, nails pressing into his palm.","\"You know... it was just a small attack. Done by a single man. Nothing special. I just wanted to show you what I am capable of. This was just a small picture... you don’t know what things I am planning for you... I will slowly destroy the things that you care about... that you owned... and then finally you...\"","A faint shadow passed through Adrian’s eyes. For a brief moment, something deeper flickered within them. It was anger. But it was controlled. He suppressed it. His breathing remained steady.","\"For now, enjoy your remaining next few peaceful days... because they won’t be peaceful for much longer.\"","With a smile, the man said, \"Bye.\"","The video ended.","The blue light that was hovering above vanished instantly. The room fell silent again.","Adrian remained sitting there, unmoving. His eyes were still fixed on the empty space where the screen had been.","His expression was calm. But the slight tightening of his jaw, and the faint crease between his brows. They spoke otherwise.","Adrian remained seated for a long moment after the video ended, his hand still resting on the now lifeless device.","The faint blue glow had vanished, leaving the room dim and heavy with silence.","Slowly, he leaned back in his chair. A long breath escaped his lips. \"...Haaah.\"","He closed his eyes and rubbed his temples again, this time more firmly, as if trying to push away the growing weight in his mind.","\"There’s no way he’s just doing this for revenge...\" he muttered under his breath, his voice low and thoughtful.","His brows furrowed deeply.","\"If it was only revenge... he wouldn’t move like this. Not after all these years.\"","Adrian opened his eyes again. The calmness in them had returned, but beneath that calm surface, there was a sharp intensity.","\"What are you trying to achieve, Malrick...?\" he whispered.","His fingers tapped lightly against the armrest of the chair, a habit he had when thinking deeply.","\"Where were you all these years... and why now?\"","His gaze shifted toward the window behind his desk. The night outside was quiet, almost too quiet, as if the world itself was unaware of the storm that had begun.","He leaned forward slightly, resting his elbows on the desk, intertwining his fingers.","\"An attack on the academy... using a controlled body... creating a barrier strong enough to stop even me...\"","His eyes narrowed.","\"And killing some students to give me pressure..\"","A faint, almost invisible frown appeared on his face. \"You are planning something bigger.\"","He leaned back again, his expression turning colder. \"This wasn’t just to hurt me... this was preparation.\"","Buzz... Buzz... Buzz...","The communication device on his desk lit up again, vibrating continuously. Adrian glanced at it briefly, irritation flashing across his eyes before it was suppressed.","He picked it up and answered calmly. He already knew who it might belong to.","\"Yes.\"","A voice came from the other side, hurried and tense. It was one of the higher authorities.","Afterall he need to give reply to others.","---","[A/N: Hello guys I made some changes in last Chapter. Where he had got Frozen Lotus Sword Art. I changed it to Frozen Lotus Blade Art.","Just wanted to informed you so you won’t feel confused later. Bye!]"]},{"number":57,"title":"Chapter 57: Weight Of Responsibility (2)","paragraphs":["A voice came from the other side, hurried and tense. It was one of the higher authorities.","\"Principal Adrian, we need an immediate explanation regarding today’s incident. Parents are already filing complaints, and some are demanding accountability—\"","\"I am aware,\" Adrian interrupted calmly, though his tone carried authority.","\"We are currently assessing the situation. A full report will be provided soon.\"","\"That is not enough. Do you realize the scale of what has happened? Students are dead—\"","\"I said I am aware,\" Adrian repeated, this time his voice slightly colder.","There was a brief silence from the other side.","Adrian continued, his tone now steady but firm.","\"The academy will take full responsibility where it is due. But right now, my priority is ensuring the safety of the remaining students and preventing another incident.\"","\"...Understood.\"","The call ended. Adrian placed the device back on the table slowly.","For a moment, he just stared at it. Then another call came. The information about this incident traveled fast.","Mostly because of other students who already informed their parents about this incident.","Many students being children of high ranking family. While some parents of dead students calling.","For the next several minutes, Adrian remained occupied, answering questions, giving controlled responses, and dealing with pressure from influential figures.","Each call demanded answers.Each call carried blame, fear, or anger.","Yet Adrian’s expression barely changed.","He remained calm. With controlled and unshaken heart he handled everything.","But once the calls finally stopped. Silence returned to the room.","Adrian exhaled again, this time more deeply. His shoulders relaxed slightly, but his eyes remained sharp.","\"Weak...\"","He muttered the word quietly. \"That’s what he’ll think of this.\"","His gaze drifted downward. \"A single man entered... killed students...\"","His fingers clenched slightly. \"And I couldn’t stop it...but I observed the barrier well...it will take few days to decode it...next time it won’t work.\"","Adrian well knew the capabilities Malrick possessed. When it came to magic, he excelled Adrian.","Forming a barrier that couldn’t let anyone enter... not even him... only he could create something like that.","That’s why, when he first touched the barrier, he understood the one who might be behind it.","It was made for especially Adrian to not enter, or anyone who was less strong than him.","Only someone stronger than Adrian could break it.","For the first time, a faint trace of frustration appeared on his face. But it disappeared just as quickly.","Emotions had no place here.","He stood up slowly from his chair and walked toward the window.","Looking out into the dark academy grounds, he spoke softly. \"I failed them.\"","A brief silence followed. Then his expression hardened again.","\"But I won’t fail again.\"","He turned back toward the desk, his movements now decisive.","\"I need information.\"","His mind began organizing everything rapidly.","\"The one who fought that man... those students...\"","\"Damien... Regnar... Draven... Arisha... Lyria...and Noah\"","He recalled their names one by one.","\"They saw him up close. Fought him directly.\"","His eyes narrowed slightly. \"They might have noticed something... anything unusual.\"","He walked back to his desk and picked up another device, activating it.","\"Prepare a report on the students involved in the battle at the eastern sector and bring it to me,\" he ordered.","\"And arrange for me to meet them once they recover.\"","A voice responded immediately, \"Yes, Principal.\"","The device went silent again. Adrian stood there for a moment, thinking. Then his gaze slowly shifted back to the black metallic device on his desk.","His eyes turned cold.","\"Malrick...\"","He spoke the name quietly. \"This time... I won’t wait.\"","The room fell silent once again. But this time it wasn’t the silence of exhaustion. It was the silence before a storm.","---","It was Monday.","Noah and the others had rested the night of Saturday and half of Sunday.","Now it was Monday, and classes were going to start as usual.","But that didn’t mean the atmosphere of the Academy was like usual.","It was more gloomy, filled with fear.","The Academy was filled with so many strong individuals, and even a principal who was one of the strongest people in the world.","Yet someone had entered and brought chaos. Many students died. Most of them belonged to the first year.","It was as if the man who planned this chose a time when mostly first years were present in that area at that time,","who were not too strong or experienced, so easy to hunt.","The classroom was silent,","not like other days when it was filled with chattering.","Noah sat on the back bench of the classroom,","while the main characters sat at the front.","It was a sad thing for Noah that Regnar and Draven weren’t in his class.","They were in B-2 class.","Noah really thought that he could be good friends with them.","Just then, the sound of heels clicking against the floor came into the silent classroom.","It pulled Noah out of his thoughts.","He looked forward at the blackboard, where Morgana Celestine was standing with her cold expression.","Today, her hair was tied in a bun. She was wearing a white shirt with long sleeves rolled up, the end of her shirt neatly tucked inside her black trousers.","She looked as beautiful and attractive as always.","But today, even Noah didn’t feel like admiring it.","The current situation was just too bad for him to be normal.","\"As you all know... we lost some of our friends on Saturday. It was an incident that no one had ever thought about...\"","Her amethyst eyes traveled over the students calmly. A few lowered their heads, while others clenched their fists.","\"As for not being able to save our students and workers... the Principal has already apologized to all of you in the auditorium yesterday...\"","Noah listened to her words, knowing about it.","Since he and the others were recovering, they didn’t attend it.","But they had heard about it.","Morgana paused for a moment, her gaze hardening slightly.","\"But remember this, students... take this as a lesson.\"","The room grew even quieter.","\"This is exactly why you must train harder... become stronger. Because the next time someone attacks you... no one may come to save you.\"","A student swallowed nervously. Another looked down at their trembling hands.","\"You will have to defend yourselves... and if needed...\"","Her voice turned colder.","\"Kill your enemies.\"","A faint chill spread through the classroom.","\"The world is not a peaceful place. Remember that.\" Her eyes sharpened as she looked at each of them. \"It is cruel... and unpredictable.\"","She straightened slightly, her voice rising with authority. \"So you will give it your all.\"","After that she sighed.","Then she contiued with serious voice.\"We won’t have any lecture for today...also the VR-battle you guys were supposed to have this week is postponed for next two weeks. We decided to give you more time to recover from this incident, also to cool down things. But your classes and training will continue like always.\"","The VR battle was postponed further. Noah didn’t care about VR Battle. He leaned back agaisnt the bench. While he continued to hear her words. Even Noah was not good mood today."]},{"number":58,"title":"Chapter 58: Going to Meet Principal.","paragraphs":["She continued her speech. After that, she said something that drew Noah’s attention.","\"Student Damien Ashworth, Arisha Willow, Lyria Sunweave, Leonard Valtier, and Noah Eldritch... you all were the ones who handled the situation and fought against the enemy. So you have been summoned by the Principal. After this lecture, go and meet him.\"","’Oh! Talk with Principal Adrian.’ Noah nodded as he was slightly interested in meeting the Principal.","After that, Morgana left the class.","’It’s time to meet the Principal, I guess.’","---","Tap.","Tap.","Tap.","Noah, Lyria, Leonard, and Arisha were walking toward the Principal’s office.","They were walking through the hallway. It was empty currently, since some other classes might have lectures","While among this group no one spoke. There was silence withing them But the silence was soon broken by Noah.","With a casual expression, he looked sideways and asked, \"So... you guys are already good friends?\"","He had nothing to talk about, so he chose a random topic.","With a slight smirk, Leonard replied, \"Well, we are. It was not hard to become friends since we were all top-ranking students. Strong ones come together faster.\"","His blonde hair was neatly combed, both hands tucked into his pockets.","The guy was more normal compared to the other gloomy students.","Not only him, but even Arisha and the others were not that bothered by the incident.","Not because they were insensitive, but because they knew they couldn’t afford to be weak. Just because of the deaths of students they didn’t even know.","It was amusing how strong they were, not only physically but mentally as well.","They were walking side by side. Leonard was on the far right. On his left was Damien.","On Damien’s left side was Lyria.","Today, she had woven her golden-blonde hair into a single, thick braid that cascaded down her back, nearly reaching her waist.","The sunlight streaming through the tall hallway windows caught every strand, making it shimmer with a rich, lustrous glow.","Her soft pink eyes held a gentle warmth, and her fair skin seemed to radiate an even brighter, almost luminous quality in the morning light.","Her figure was something that Noah could admire for hours.","’What a sight... she is really beautiful... befitting for being the female lead.’","Beside Lyria was Arisha.","Noah walked beside Arisha, their footsteps echoing softly down the corridor.","She moved with effortless grace, the first-year uniform fitting her tall curvious frame perfectly.","The ash gray blazer with its sharp red piping hugged her shoulders and waist, while the pleated skirt swayed gently around her long legs with every step, the fabric whispering against her skin.","Her striking violet hair cascaded down her back in rich, lustrous waves, catching the light like spilled ink laced with amethyst. At nearly 175 centimeters, she stood noticeably taller than most of the other first-years, her posture straight and regal.","A pair of cool, yellow eyes gazed forward with quiet indifference, sharp and luminous beneath long lashes. Her skin was pale and flawless, almost luminous, like fine porcelain under moonlight smooth, unblemished, and carrying an almost ethereal quality.","And about her figure, Noah didn’t even want to think about that.","With a calm but slightly sharp tone, Arisha asked while still looking forward, \"What are you staring at, Noah?\"","Noah didn’t stop looking at her. He continued to admire her beauty while walking ahead.","With a shameless calm expression, he replied, \"You already know... why are you asking then?\"","His crystal-like blue eyes were calm like the ocean. There was no bad intention in them.","With wide eyes, Leonard exclaimed, \"Damn! You really said that!\"","Damien didn’t comment. He simply watched from the side with curiosity.","Lyria glanced at Noah, then at Arisha, and then back at Noah, surprised.","Arisha turned her eyes toward Noah, meeting his blue gaze.","With her usual indifferent tone, she said, \"Hmm... just because you are handsome doesn’t mean it will work on me. So don’t waste your time.\"","For a moment there was silence again.","Leonard blinked.","Damien’s brows lifted slightly.","Even Lyria’s soft pink eyes widened a little.","Under his breath, Leonard muttered in disbelief, \"...Did she just say handsome?\"","That single word echoed in their minds more than Noah’s shameless reply.","Noah himself seemed slightly surprised for a brief second.","Then a small smile appeared on his face.","He finally looked forward, his expression calm and relaxed.","With a casual tone, he said, \"Thanks for saying I am handsome. But I was not trying to hit on you... even if you are extremely beautiful.\"","This time, Lyria’s eyes widened even more.","Leonard almost choked on air.","Damien quietly observed, a faint hint of amusement appearing in his eyes.","Without missing a beat, Arisha replied while looking forward, \"Look, you are trying again.\"","Noah raised an eyebrow slightly, his expression still calm.","With a steady voice, he said, \"What trying? By no means I am trying to impress or flirt with you. I was just stating the truth.\"","Leonard stopped walking for half a second.","In a low voice, he whispered, \"...This guy is insane,\" and then quickly caught up.","Lyria looked between Noah and Arisha, clearly confused by how casually both of them were speaking.","Everyone knew that Arisha didn’t have a good impression of children from noble families, except for a few she personally knew.","By the reputation Noah possessed, they were surprised why she was acting so casually toward him.","Even Noah was surprised at first, but he simply thought her personality was just too cool.","Damien, on the other hand, crossed his arms slightly as he walked, observing Noah with interest.","With a calm and curious tone, Damien said, \"You really don’t hesitate to say anything, do you?\"","Noah shrugged lightly. \"If it’s true, then why hesitate?\"","Arisha glanced at him once more from the corner of her eyes.","For a brief moment, there was no change in her expression, but something flickered in her eyes.","Then it disappeared instantly.","\"You talk too much,\" she said simply.","\"And you listen too nicely,\" Noah replied without missing a chance."]},{"number":59,"title":"Chapter 59: Meeting Principal.","paragraphs":["Leonard let out a quiet laugh.","With a grin, he said, \"Okay, I like this guy now.\"","Lyria, still trying to process everything, said softly, \"You two are... strange.\"","With a playful tone, Leonard corrected, \"Yeah... they are strange. We are normal.\"","Damien shook his head slightly but said nothing more.","After a brief pause, Noah spoke again, curiosity in his tone.","\"By the way... I was curious... I heard you don’t like noble young masters... then why are you nic— I mean, why are you okay with me? Is it because I am handsome?\"","For the first time, Arisha’s expression changed.","A faint frown appeared on her face.","With a slightly annoyed tone, she said, \"Now you are sounding narcissistic.\"","Then she continued calmly, \"The reason why I am okay with you is simple. First, you beat that idiot guy who was trying to insult a girl in the cafeteria...\"","She paused briefly before continuing,","\"Then... how you fought against the enemy rather than running away. Together with others... that puts you as a good comrade for us.\"","Her voice remained steady as she added,","\"Lastly... you are exiled... no longer a noble. Just a commoner like me.\"","Those last words felt like an arrow striking his heart.","Noah’s expression didn’t change much, but something inside him shifted.","Then he let out a small laugh.","\"Haha! Okay... thanks, I guess. Now I think we could be good friends since we are both commoners.\"","The others listened quietly.","With a calm expression, Damien said, \"I don’t know what you have done in the past or why you acted that way before... but right now... you seem like a better person to me as well, Noah.\"","Lyria nodded gently.","With a soft smile, she said, \"Every person can change if they put their mind into it... I believe Noah has changed.\"","Leonard scratched his cheek awkwardly.","\"I kind of like this guy’s new personality. He was such a bas— I mean... he really had a bad personality before.\"","He quickly corrected himself.","Noah understood, but he didn’t say anything.","A small smile formed on his face.","’It seems my reputation is at least getting better among these guys.’","\"Thanks, guys...\"","The group continued walking through the long hallway, sunlight streaming through the tall windows, casting long shadows on the polished floor.","Their footsteps echoed softly.","For a moment, the atmosphere felt lighter than before.","Tap.","Tap.","Heavy footsteps echoed from behind. All of them instinctively turned around. From the other end of the hallway.","Two figures were approaching.","One of them was extremely tall, easily around or even over 200 cm. His broad frame and muscular build made him stand out instantly.","It was Draven.","Beside him walked Regnar, his light gray hair slightly messy, and his tiger-like ears twitching faintly as he moved.","Both of them still had some bandages visible, but their presence remained as imposing as ever.","Noah’s face lit up immediately.","A wide smile spread across his face as he raised his hand and waved energetically.","\"Oi! Over here!\" he called out loudly. \"Come here, my friends!\"","Leonard blinked again.","\"...Friends already?\"","Regnar noticed them and smirked slightly.","Draven simply looked at them with his usual calm expression.","They walked closer, their heavy and steady steps echoing in the hallway.","With a casual tone, Regnar greeted, \"Yo. You guys heading to the Principal too?\"","Noah nodded with a grin.","\"Yeah. Got summoned.\"","Draven crossed his arms slightly, looking at the group.","\"Same,\" he said briefly.","Lyria gave a gentle nod.","\"Good to see you both are fine.\"","Regnar chuckled.","\"Fine? I was better yesterday. But yeah... still alive.\"","Draven glanced at Noah for a moment.","\"You did well.\"","Simple words. But they carried weight. Noah scratched the back of his head lightly.","\"We all did.\"","Arisha remained silent, but her gaze briefly shifted toward Draven and Regnar, acknowledging them.","Damien stepped forward slightly. \"Let’s not keep the Principal waiting.\"","Everyone nodded.","Without wasting more time, the group of seven turned and started walking together toward the Principal’s office.","Their footsteps echoed in unison now.","A group that had fought together. Survived together. And now, they were about to face something far more serious.","The group walked through the long corridor in silence once again, their footsteps echoing faintly against the polished floor.","Soon, they reached a large wooden door at the end of the hallway.","The door was grand, carved with intricate patterns, giving off a heavy and authoritative presence.","Above it was a simple metal plate.","Principal’s Office.","Everyone slowed down slightly as they approached. A faint tension settled over the group.","Even Leonard, who was usually relaxed, straightened his posture a bit.","Damien stepped forward, his expression calm and composed.","He raised his hand and knocked on the door.","Knock.","Knock.","He opened his mouth to speak. \"We—\"","But before he could finish. A deep, authoritative voice came from inside.","\"You all can come in.\" It was heavy and cold.","The group exchanged brief glances.","Damien didn’t hesitate.He placed his hand on the handle and pushed the door open.","Creak.","The door opened slowly. They stepped inside. First Damien, then others behind him.","The office was spacious and well-organized. Tall bookshelves lined the walls, filled with countless books and documents.","A large window behind the desk allowed soft light to enter, illuminating the room.","At the center, behind a large wooden desk sat Adrian.","He wore a beige-colored shirt and black pants. His posture was straight.","His black eyes were calm, yet cold and authoritative.","The moment they entered. His gaze moved across each of them. His gaze was sharp, observant and measuring.","The group instinctively stood straighter as they approached the desk.","No one spoke. No one moved unnecessarily. They stopped in front of him in a line. For a brief moment silence filled the room.","Then, Adrian leaned back slightly in his chair, his expression unreadable.","His eyes rested on them one by one. Finally in a calm but heavy voice, he spoke, \"Good to see you all are recovered.\""]},{"number":60,"title":"Chapter 60: Talk with Principal","paragraphs":["\"Humble are we? Thats good attitude. Now i won’t take much of your time. I just wanted to hear the incident frok you guys directly. That’s why i didnt send anyone else to inquiry you about whatever happen there\"","All seven students stood side by side in front of Adrian’s desk.","They bowed respectfully before standing straight once again.","Noah was standing at the far left end. The man sitting in front of them was Adrian Aegeus. One of the people who had reached Sovereign Core.","One of the strongest individuals in the world. That did not mean there was no one stronger than him. There were still a few others who were even stronger than Adrian.","Adrian folded his hands together on top of the desk, his sharp black eyes observing every single one of them carefully.","\"Firstly, I thank every one of you for fighting with such courage and for killing the person who was behind this incident. You all fought bravely. I am proud of you all.\"","Damien slightly lowered his head before replying in a calm voice.","\"Thank you for your compliment, Sir Adrian. But we all only did what was important at that time. We did everything to survive.\"","A faint smile appeared on Adrian’s face. \"Humble, are we? That is a good attitude.\" His eyes surveyed over everyone. They were standing straight without any arrogance on their face.","Then his expression turned serious again.","\"Now, I will not take much of your time. I simply wanted to hear about the incident directly from you all. That is why I did not send anyone else to question you regarding what happened there.\"","The seven students listened to him quietly. For a brief moment, no one spoke. They glanced at each other, silently deciding who should speak first.","Finally, Damien took one step forward.","His posture remained straight as he began speaking.","\"I will start first.\"","Adrian gave a small nod, allowing him to continue.","Damien took a short breath.","\"Me,Lyria, Arisha, and Leonard were walking through one of the streets together. Everything seemed normal at first. There was nothing wrong. Students were chatting and laughing. While workers doing their work.\"","His hazel eyes narrowed slightly as he recalled the memory. \"Then suddenly, the space between the road tore, a huge portal opened in front of us out of nowhere.\"","The room remained silent as everyone listened.","\"Monsters immediately started coming out from inside it. A lot of them.\"","Lyria softly lowered her gaze while remembering that moment.","Damien continued.","\"There was no time to think. We started fighting right away because the monsters were already attacking nearby students.\"","He calmly explained how they had engaged in battle. How Leonard used his attacks to keep monsters away from injured students. How Arisha supported them with her healing and also killing other monsters. How Arisha continuously fired arrows to control the battlefield.","How Damien himself fought at the front.","Noah listened carefully as well.","Even though he had heard parts of it before, listening now helped him understand the entire situation better.","Damien then continued until he reached the part where they had encountered the giant monster.","\"The strongest one among them was a huge monster. Much stronger than the others.\"","Adrian’s fingers tapped lightly once on the desk.","\"And then?\"","Damien’s expression hardened slightly.","\"We fought it together.\"","He explained that battle carefully. How difficult it had been. How dangerous the monster was. How they had nearly lost.","And finally how Damien had used everything he had to kill it.","He told that to kill monster he used his ability. He didn’t explain his ability, just told that it’s side effect made him unable to use mana for a while.","When Noah heard his words,he remembered just what kind of ability Damien posses.","His ability named as Solar Core. An extra core inside his body. Unlike how his normal core works and made up of mana like others.","His Solar core was made up of pure light energy...more like light mana.","In character list it was written that light mana was Lower version of devine power that belongs to Sun God.","By activating that core he get boost for his all Stats. Increasing the attack power of his all magic spells. And lastly he could bring a minture sun into existence to turned his enemy into ashes.","Noah still remembered the bright light that had filled the surroundings space during incident.","When Damien finished, Adrian remained silent for a moment.","Then he asked in a calm voice,","\"Did any of you notice something strange or suspicious before the portal appeared?\"","The four of them thought carefully.","Lyria gently shook her head first.","\"No, Sir.\"","Leonard crossed his arms while thinking deeply.\"Nothing unusual from my side either. Me and Lyria were killing monsters. While Arisha and others started to fight that guy Petrick.\"","Arisha calmly replied as well. \"I noticed nothing suspicious as well.\"","Damien gave the final answer. \"Same for me.\"","Adrian nodded slowly. \"I see.\"","His gaze then moved toward Regnar and Draven.","\"You two.\"","Regnar scratched the side of his cheek before stepping forward together with Draven.","This time Regnar started speaking.","\"Me and Draven were eating at a food stall on the road.\"","Draven silently nodded beside him.","\"Then monsters suddenly appeared there too.\"","Regnar explained how chaos had started in their area as well.","How civilians and students began panicking. How he and Draven immediately started fighting. How they kept holding the monsters back.","Draven then added in his deep voice, \"We focused on protecting nearby students first.\"","Regnar smile slightly. \"Yeah, and while fighting lizard like monster we met Noah. He helped us by throwing his spear at monster’s front.\"","Adrian’s eyes shifted toward Noah for a brief moment before returning to them.","Regnar continued. \"He came to help us fight.\"","Draven spoke again.","\"After that we saw Damien’s group fighting a powerful monster from a distance.\"","Regnar nodded.","\"That is when things got messier. I think its better if Noah explained it further.\"","They explained everything until the moment Noah suggested finding the person controlling everything.","When they finished speaking, Adrian remained thoughtful.","Finally, his black eyes moved toward Noah.","\"And now your side.\"","For some reason, Noah felt slightly more nervous when Adrian directly looked at him.","Still, he stepped forward.","He took a slow breath. Then began speaking. \"I was at a café.\"","Everyone quietly listened.","\"When the attack started, the building suddenly broke apart.\"","He explained how chaos had erupted around him. How he had escaped outside. How he later met Regnar and Draven. How the three of them started fighting together. Noah’s voice remained steady as he continued.","His blue eyes narrowed slightly while recalling everything.","\"While everyone was focused on battle against monster, I thought someone had to be controlling this.\"","Adrian leaned slightly forward in his chair.","Noah noticed that but continued.","\"So we started searching.\"","He then explained how he had carefully observed the surroundings. How he had thought the enemy would likely choose a place with a good view. How that led him to inspect nearby buildings.","\"And then I found him.\"","The room felt slightly heavier now.","\"On the terrace of a cake shop.\"","Leonard blinked.","Even now, hearing Noah describe it calmly felt strange considering how insane that fight had been.","Noah continued telling everything in detail. How Petrick had been standing there.","How the battle escalated. How Regnar and Draven joined him. How Arisha and Damiene eventually arrived too.","Then Noah described Petrick himself.","\"The way he fought...\" Noah paused briefly.","His expression turned serious.","\"He was too experienced.\"","Adrian’s eyes sharpened slightly.","Noah continued.","\"It felt like fighting someone who had gone through countless battles.\"","He explained Petrick’s strange power. His sudden increase in strength.","Then Noah carefully told Adrian about Petrick seemingly burning his own life force for power.","That part made Adrian’s expression change ever so slightly. Noah noticed it. But he kept going. Finally he explained the end of the battle. How they created the opening together. How Regnar used Sound Burst. How the mist covered everything. And how Noah landed the final attack.","But he didn’t stop there. After telling all of this he finally told him about how it was not Petrick who was doing all of this. It was someone else who was controlling Petrick’s body like Puppet from afar. How Noah ahead came to that conclusion.","When Noah finished speaking, silence filled the office.","Adrian remained seated behind his desk.","His fingers were folded together near his mouth now.His sharp black eyes studied all seven students deeply.","The room had become completely quiet. Because now Adrian was thinking. Very seriously.","---","The group had left Adrian’s office.","After hearing everything, he came to understand who might be the one working with Malrick.","Adrian’s expression turned serious.","\"There is only one person I know... who could control someone else’s body and manipulate them like a puppet while placing his own consciousness inside them.\"","He leaned on his desk.","Both his elbows rested on the table, his hands locked together while his chin rested on them.","His black eyes narrowed deeply.","Then they sparkled with realization.","There was only one person possessing an ability like that.","\"Cassian Nightfall... after vanishing for more than ten years... I am hearing about him for the first time... just like Malrick.\" He said with serious voice.","\"So he joined hands with Malrick....\"","His brows slowly furrowed. A heavy silence filled the office. His expression darkened further.","\"What are they planning.\""]},{"number":61,"title":"Chapter 61: Forgive me this one time!\"","paragraphs":["After a while, everyone stepped out of the office.","They started walking through the hallway.","With a wide smile on his face, Noah checked his mobile and said, \"Now... that was an amazing reward we got there.\"","With a slightly dissatisfied expression, Regnar flicked one of his tiger-like ears and commented, \"What amazing? I thought we might get something more special... but it’s just extra Nova Points.\"","With his usual slow tone, Draven looked at Regnar and said, \"Dude, we got 5,00,000 Nova Points. Each of us got that much with good credit points. And you think it was nothing?\"","With a huge grin, Noah waved his mobile slightly and said, \"Damn, I am gonna enjoy this month with this much money. I mean points. Haha\"","He was the happiest among them after getting this many points.","Currently, Noah was an exiled son. Draven was from a tribe where money was not very important. Damien and Arisha were commoners.","So only these four had reason to be happy.","Except Damien, the other three were acting normal, as if they did not care much about the reward.","While Leonard and Lyria were from rich families.","This many points did not mean much to them.","Of course, Noah could just call his father and get money.","But it still felt awkward to do that.","Asking money from him while Noah himself didn’t feel any attachment or family-like feelings toward him and the other family members.","So he wouldn’t ask for money unless it was necessary and important.","He could get shameless when it was needed.","With a smirk, Leonard glanced at Noah and said, \"By the way... you are smarter than I thought... the way you act doesn’t give the feeling that you can deduct things so well.\"","Noah frowned at Leonard’s comment.","Clicking his tongue, Noah replied, \"Tch! When it’s necessary, I do act serious and know how to use my brain to the fullest.\"","Then, with a casual shrug, he added, \"But other times I just be normal. No need to act like some mysterious kind of character who is smart and cool.\"","As he said that, Noah moved closer toward Lyria.","With an easy smile, he asked, \"By the way, Lyria... you free tomorrow?\"","Lyria looked at Noah with her soft pink eyes. Some of her golden blonde hair strands frame her forehead. Her sweet face could make anyone feel calm.","With a gentle expression, she said, \"Well... I don’t have anything to do... at least after tomorrow’s lectures end. I mean if lectures do happen tomorrow. Mostly I will study in the library or train.\"","As she spoke, she tilted her head in a cute way.","Her response made Noah nod his head.","With a satisfied smile, he said, \"Perfect. Let’s go on a date tomorrow in the late afternoon. Everything on me.\" He said casually, as if it was no hig deal.","His response made Lyria visibly flinch.","Her cheeks turned a shade of pink in embarrassment.","With wide eyes, she stammered, \"Wh-wh-what are y-you saying!?\"","With surprise clearly visible on his face, Damien exclaimed, \"What?\"","Chuckling in amusement, Leonard said, \"That’s too bold.\"","With his tiger-like ears standing straight up, Regnar stared at Noah and said, \"How can you be so direct?\"","With complete seriousness, Draven nodded once and said, \"Noah is a real man. So forward and brave.\"","Clicking her tongue softly, Arisha crossed her arms and said, \"Tch! He moved from me to another woman so fast.\"","Once again, Arisha’s words made everyone even more baffled.","Laughing cheerfully, Noah said to Lyria, ignoring the comments made by others,\"Hehehe! Come on, don’t be so surprised. It’s not like a beautiful lady like you was never asked on a date before.\"","Still blushing heavily, Lyria quickly replied, \"O-of course not! No one ever asked me on a date before! And how could you ask this out if nowhere.\"","Noah stared at her in disbelief.","\"What the hell? How is that possible? Damn, I am wondering what all men are doing if they never tried to get closer to you. Such cowards.\"","Shaking his head with amusement, Leonard said, \"Because not everyone is like you, Noah.\"","Still flustered, Lyria lowered her gaze and stammered, \"Well... I-I... I don’t think I can—\"","But before she could finish.","Noah suddenly burst into laughter.","\"Hahaha! Oh dear Lyria, I was just joking around. Haha.\"","He casually confessed that he had only been joking.","It was not like he tried to change it before getting rejected by her on the date.","Yes, it was definitely not because of that!","He was truly joking around.","Lyria immediately froze.","Then her embarrassed face turned even redder.","Pointing at Noah with shaky fingers, she said, \"Y-you! Don’t talk to me! Hmph!\"","With her face becoming crimson, Lyria turned her face to the side with a small pout.","Chuckling softly, Noah said, \"Hehe, your reaction was just too cute and adorable.\"","Lyria clenched her fists tightly and started walking faster without looking at Noah.","She felt embarrassed every time he said something.","No one had ever talked to her like that before.","Noah then turned toward Arisha.","She was watching everything with her usual calm, indifferent face. Her soft violet hair rested against her back and shoulders","But there was a spark in her eyes.","As if she was enjoying it.","With fake smile, Noah placed a hand on his chest and said, \"There’s no way I will ever abandon Arisha and go to another girl.\"","Without changing her expression, Arisha replied, \"You lost that small chance with me. Now don’t come back.\"","Leonard rubbed his forehead and muttered, \"This is getting crazier.\"","Regnar twitched his ears and said, \"Man, Arisha does act good despite not showing any emotion.\"","Suddenly Noah reached one hand toward Arisha.","With fake despair in his voice, he cried out, \"No, Arisha! Please don’t abandon me! Please forgive me this one time!\"","He walked beside her now.","Other laughed as they watched them.","Just like that, the group moved away from Adrian’s office."]},{"number":62,"title":"Chapter 62: Consulting with Morgana","paragraphs":["After having a talk with Principal Adrian, they went back to class.","During break time, most students went back to their dormitories since no lecture was taken, and some went to train, such as Damien and others.","While Noah, he was going toward Morgana Celestine’s cabin.","The reason was simple. He wanted to join an adventurer’s guild. He wanted to take permission from her.","He had tried to read the rules, and he got to know that they could join adventurer guilds. But they needed to report to the academy before going on any mission, how many days it might take, and in which place they were going on the mission.","So in case something happened to the students or they didn’t come back in the reported time, the academy would know.","Noah came to her cabin and stood outside.","He remembered how he and those three idiots were brought here by a senior.","\"Huff... calm down, Noah. Why are you nervous to talk with her? Your reputation is good now. No need to worry.\"","He knocked on the door.","The door was not huge and grand like Principal Adrian’s. It was just a normal door.","Knock","\"Instructor Morgana. It’s Noah. Can I come in?\"","There was silence, but then her strict voice came.","\"You may enter.\"","Noah pushed the door open.","Inside the instructor’s office, Morgana sat behind the desk with elegant poise. Her sky-blue hair was neatly arranged in a sleek bun, with a single loose bang gracefully framing the side of her face.","She wore a crisp white long-sleeved blouse that perfectly accentuated the generous curves of her breasts. Her skin was flawlessly smooth and fair, almost luminous under the soft lighting. Her striking amethyst eyes held their usual icy authority.","Noah stood frozen for a moment, simply staring at her in a daze. In class, when his mood had been foul, he had barely noticed her beauty. But now, in the quiet of her office, he couldn’t look away. She was breathtaking.","Morgana remained focused on the documents in front of her for a few seconds longer.","Then, slowly, she lifted her gaze to meet his. As always, her amethyst eyes were cold and strict, carrying the sharp weight of authority.","Both of them stared at each other for a while.","Watching Noah not saying anything, she decided to break the silence.","\"What is it, Noah? Why did you come here to meet me? Don’t tell me you just came here to stare.\"","At her words, Noah came out of his trance.","By no means was Noah some man who only thought about women.","In his last life, he was not like this. But the women of this world were just too beautiful that he couldn’t help but get mesmerized by them.","In the end, he was just a twenty-year-old guy in his last life, and nineteen years old here.","He didn’t have any experience with women of this appearance.","’People were crazy for actresses for no reason... the women of this world are just on a crazy level.’","Noah walked toward her desk and asked permission. \"Can I sit here?\"","She observed his handsome face, which was nothing special in her eyes.","\"Hmm... you can... but do you want to talk about something long that you are asking to sit?\"","Noah pulled one of the two chairs in front of her desk and sat comfortably on it. He gave her his signature fak– his signature true smile.","The gentle smile just looked too charming on his handsome face.","\"It’s not something that would take too much of your time.\"","\"Okay... then what is it?\"","\"Actually, I wanted to join an adventurer’s guild. I came to inform you and, well... kind of wanted advice from you. If you know any good guild that I could join. Also, if there are any rules about this that I might not know, then I would be grateful for your help.\"","She leaned back against her chair. Her fingers tapped on the desk.","Morgana leaned back against her chair, her fingers tapping lightly on the polished wooden desk. The soft, rhythmic sound filled the silence for a moment as she studied Noah carefully.","Her amethyst eyes narrowed slightly, not in suspicion, but in evaluation.","\"...An adventurer’s guild, huh...\" she murmured, almost to herself.","Noah remained silent, sitting straight yet relaxed, waiting for her response. He didn’t interrupt. He knew better than that.","After a brief pause, she folded her arms loosely beneath her chest and spoke again.","\"You did your research at least. That’s good. Many students come here with half-baked ideas without even reading the academy rules.\"","Her gaze sharpened slightly.","\"As you already know, the academy allows students to join adventurer guilds. But that privilege comes with responsibility. You are not free to act recklessly outside just because you are talented.\"","Noah nodded. \"I understand.\"","She continued.","\"There are multiple guilds you can join. Most students at your level enter low to mid-tier guilds. Iron and bronze-ranked guilds are for beginners. Silver-ranked guilds handle intermediate missions. Gold-ranked guilds... are where things start to get serious.\"","Her fingers stopped tapping.","\"You are not suited for bronze,\" she said bluntly. \"It would be a waste of your ability.\"","Noah raised an eyebrow slightly but didn’t argue.","\"So your options are Silver... or lower-end Gold guilds,\" she added.","She leaned forward slightly now, resting her elbow on the desk and supporting her chin with her hand.","\"But,\" she paused, her tone shifting just a little, \"if you’re asking for my recommendation...\"","Her eyes locked onto his.","\"There is one guild.\"","Noah straightened slightly. \"The name is Crimson Eyes,\" she said.","Her voice was calm, but there was a subtle weight behind those words.","\"It is a mid-tier Gold-ranked guild. Not the strongest, but stable. Disciplined. Their members are not idiots who chase death for glory. You are still at lower core but becasue if being academy student you will be accepted there.\"","She paused briefly before adding,","\"And I know the guild master personally.\"","That alone carried a lot of meaning.","\"If you join them, you will be guided properly. You won’t be thrown into meaningless danger, and you’ll actually grow.\"","Noah listened carefully, nodding slowly.","\"I recommend you join that one,\" she concluded.","There was no hesitation in her tone. Noah smiled slightly. \"Then I’ll trust your recommendation.\"","Morgana gave a small nod.","\"Good. Also, you are near a breakthrough. I can feel it. I hope you will try to go on missions after ranking up.\"","\"As you say, Instructor.\"","Then her expression turned serious again as she continued with the rules.","\"Now listen carefully. This part is important.\"","Noah’s posture straightened.","\"If you plan to take missions, you must report to the academy beforehand. Always. You will submit where you are going, what type of mission it is, and how long you expect to be gone.\"","Her gaze hardened slightly.","\"If you fail to return within that time frame without notice, the academy will assume the worst.\"","Noah understood what that meant.","\"And,\" she continued, \"you are still a student first. Your primary responsibility is your training here.\"","She raised a finger slightly.","\"Take missions on weekends or during free periods. Do not let guild work interfere with your classes.\"","Noah nodded again. \"Understood.\"","\"If a mission requires more time,\" she added, \"you will apply for leave in advance. I will review it. If necessary, the principal will be informed.\"","She leaned back again.","\"Balance both. That is the key. If you fail at either, you will be forced to withdraw from guild activities.\"","Her tone made it clear that this wasn’t a suggestion.","Noah listened to every word carefully, committing it all to memory.","After she finished, there was a brief silence.","Then Noah stood up slowly.","\"Thank you, Instructor,\" he said sincerely. \"That was really helpful.\"","Morgana gave a small nod. \"It’s my duty.\"","She paused for a moment, then added,","\"And Noah...\"","He looked at her.","\"You did well during that incident.\"","Noah blinked slightly.","\"I heard everything from Damien,\" she continued. \"Your actions, your decisions... your composure.\"","Her eyes softened just a fraction.","\"I am impressed.\"","For a moment, Noah just stood there.","Then a genuine smile spread across his face.","\"Thank you, Instructor,\" he said, his voice lighter now.","Then, with a slight playful tone, he added,","\"Getting a compliment from a beautiful lady like you is a great honor for me.\"","Morgana stiffened. Just for a second. It was subtle. She frowned. Just when she was going to scold him,","Noah gave a respectful bow.","\"See you later, Instructor.\"","With that, he turned and walked toward the door.","He opened it, stepped out, and closed it behind him.","The room fell silent again.","Morgana remained sitting there, completely still.","Her fingers, which had always moved with control and precision, now rested motionless on the desk.","\"...This boy...\"","She muttered quietly, then rubbed her temples.","She didn’t know why, but Noah looked like a troublesome kid who would bring a lot of problems. Just like on the first day.","Then she straightened slightly, regaining her usual composed expression.","\"Hope he won’t do some idiotic things and act like a normal student.\""]},{"number":63,"title":"Chapter 63: Small Lie","paragraphs":["Noah stepped out of Morgana’s cabin with a satisfied smile on his face.","Getting a compliment from her meant his reputation was also improving in her eyes.","She had even called him talented. Though Noah himself didn’t think he was talented. But it wasn’t like that mattered to him.","Compliments were always good for Noah.","Just as he stepped out, he saw Damien coming from the opposite side.","The man looked slightly sweaty from training. His black hair was damp, with a few strands clinging to his forehead.","His hazel eyes were sharp and clear as always.","But he still looked slightly tired.","The moment those hazel eyes landed on Noah, a flicker of surprise appeared in them.","With a curious expression, Damien asked, \"Noah? What are you doing here?... Did you just come out of Master’s cabin? Was there something you wanted to discuss with her?\"","Noah smiled lightly. \"Oh, hey Damien. I came here to—\"","He suddenly paused.","He was about to tell him the reason, but stopped midway.","A small teasing smile appeared on his face.","Damien frowned slightly. \"What? You stopped talking suddenly?\"","He stood in front of Noah, looking at him with suspicion.","Noah scratched his cheek lightly, pretending hesitation. \"Actually... I don’t know if I should tell you the truth... it’s kind of something I can’t tell anyone.\"","Those words only made Damien more curious.","With a slight frown, he said, \"Hey Noah, we are practically friends now after fighting together. What’s there to hide?\"","Noah looked at him seriously. \"You sure... you won’t tell this to anyone else?\"","His expression was so natural that if he were to give an audition for a movie, he would get selected very easily.","Damien nodded firmly. \"Yes, I won’t. I promise.\"","Noah leaned in slightly, lowering his voice.","\"Good. Actually...\"","He glanced around, checking both sides to make sure no one was nearby.","Then he leaned closer and whispered, \"You see... me and Instructor Morgana... we are kind of close to each other. You know... how a man and a woman are close to each other.\"","Damien froze.","His eyes widened instantly.","\"W-what?\"","Noah nodded with a serious face.","\"Yes. I know it’s hard to believe. But... well, I just flirted with her a few days ago for fun... just like how I did with Arisha and...\"","A shy smile appeared on Noah’s face, as if he was talking about his first love.","\"She didn’t push me away... unknowingly, we got closer after some interaction. And now... we are more comfortable with each other. Just right now we talk about sweet things... and also... some intimate things... hehe~\"","He let out a soft giggle.","Damien stood there, completely stunned. His brain seemed to stop working. After a moment, he shook his head in disbelief, rubbing his chin.","\"Y-you are lying, aren’t you? My master would never get close to any man. She’s a crazy woman who only loves training and strength. A single-forever type woman.\"","He looked at Noah with a confused expression.","\"You know she has never shown any interest in men at all. I tried asking her a few times why she’s single even at this age. She always said that she’s not interested in it... and now you’re saying she’s interested in you? Why?\"","Noah stepped closer again and whispered dramatically, \"I don’t know what things she says to you... but she said... she thinks I am cute and really handsome... and also that she actually likes cute things. And now we two are hehe~\"","Noah once again giggled shyly.","\"Hey, Damien, please don’t tell this to anyone.\"","Then Noah straightened up and started walking away.","After taking a few steps, he suddenly stopped.","He turned back, placed his right hand on Damien’s left shoulder, and gave him a big, confident smile.","\"We are already at the stage where... there is no stop. Also... from now on, show some respect to me... after all, I am not just a friend of yours or a student... but also your master’s man.\"","With that, Noah turned around again and walked away, casually whistling.","Leaving behind a completely confused and stunned Damien.","With a stunned expression, he entered Morgana’s office, only to get scolded by her for not showing respect by knocking on the door first.","---","Inside a training room.","It was big enough for one person to practice.","The walls and floor were made up of light gray, strong metal that could not be broken easily by attacks.","In the middle of the room sat Noah.","These were training rooms where students could train without any disturbance. But they needed to book a slot for it, since there were just too many students.","He sat cross-legged, doing meditation.","He guided the raw mana toward his core and began refining it as he circulated it, making it adaptable to his body.","His breathing became slightly uneven. Sweat began forming along his forehead. The refining process demanded focus.","Then he imagined accumulating the purified mana around his core, forming a thin layer over it.","This process was for gradually increasing core density and capacity.","He tried to compress the accumulated layer, condensing it, then pressing it tighter.","The pressure increased. A dull ache formed in his lower abdomen.","His jaw clenched unconsciously. More sweat dripped down his neck.","After meditating for a while, he stopped.","\"Haff.. haf...\" He breathed heavily.","’At this rate... it will take more time to break through... I have been doing meditation to increase my mana for hours each day since coming to this world... but it’s slow.’","Noah looked forward and opened his status.","===STATUS===","Name: Noah Eldritch","Race: Human","Age: 19 years","Strength: 88","Speed: 75","Stamina: 91","Endurance: 72","Charm: 510","Mana: 802","Core Rank: Dormant (High)","Potential: Refined Core (High)","Profession: [Combatant Lvl.1]","Technique: None","Affinity: Ice","Spells: [Ice Shard], [Frost Bind]","Innate Ability: Ice Creation","===","A look of surprise appeared on his face.","\"That’s... too much improvement than I thought,\" he muttered under his breath.","It hadn’t been too long since he came to this world. Despite training for hours each day, the progression was much more than he had anticipated.","\"But... it’s still not enough to break through... I... I need mana cores... or rather, monster cores... which can help me absorb mana from them... and help me level up fast.\"","He sighed.","It wasn’t like he hadn’t tried to get one. Before, it was because of money that he didn’t buy any.","The cheapest cores were E-rank monster cores.","Which were pretty useless even for those who were at the Dormant Core stage.","For Noah, F-rank mana cores would be useful, but he would need many of them. While D-rank mana cores would be best, they were out of his budget.","He was thinking of talking to his father for money.","But now he had Nova points, from which he could purchase some cores. One of the reasons for joining the Adventurers Guild was to hunt monsters, take their cores, and also purchase cores from the guild.","\"I will visit it tomorrow... for now... let’s practice my blade art for the first time,\" he said with excitement.","He was eager to learn this five-star blade art."]},{"number":64,"title":"Chapter 64: Frozen Lotus Blade Art","paragraphs":["Noah stood in the middle of the room.","He decided to use a sword for learning this art.","Frozen Lotus Blade Art was an art that could be performed by any weapon that had a blade.","Be it a sword, spear, axe, dagger, or scythe, etc. No matter which weapon it might be, as long as it had a blade to cut, the blade art could be used with those weapons.","’It has eight petals...’ Noah thought while trying to understand this art.","He had gotten all the information about this blade art. It was divided into eight forms. Each form was called by the number of petals.","Such as the first form.","Frozen Lotus Blade Art: First Petal – Dewdrop Stance","’Alright, let’s do it...’","The first form focused more on stance rather than strike.","It was not meant to fight with. It was meant to prepare for the fight. The stance itself was the technique. The way the body was positioned, the way breathing was controlled, the way mana flowed inward rather than outward. All of that was the skill being practiced.","Noah exhaled softly.","He stood still on his feet, the sword held in his right hand.","Before the lotus blooms. It gathers water.","That’s what this form meant. Noah couldn’t understand what it actually entailed.","He decided to perform it.","The instructions were simple enough. Hold the blade with both hands, gripping the hilt firmly. Position it back and downward behind the body, tip pointing backward or downward toward the ground. Body turned slightly sideways. Weight distributed and ready to launch forward.","It worked the same for other weapons. They just needed to hold it slightly downward behind them.","Noah shifted his feet. Left foot forward. Right foot back. He brought the sword back and down behind his right side.","Both hands were on the hilt now, grip firm, blade angled low so the tip aimed toward the floor. He turned his shoulders slightly sideways. Bent his knees.","Noah breathed in slowly through his nose.","’Now draw the mana inward.’","He reached for his ice affinity the way the manual instructed. Not pushing outward the way he always had, but pulling inward.","Gathering. The cool pressure that lived in his core, that familiar sensation he had carried for many years like a stone kept close, he tried to redirect it. He aimed it toward his right shoulder. Coaxed it downward through his arm.","It did not move.","He breathed out. Breathed in again. Then he tried harder.","The mana sat in his core like it always did, present, aware, completely uninterested in his instructions, at least for now.","He exhaled sharply through his teeth.","He reset his stance. His shoulders back. Sword in a low position. He was in complete stillness.","He tried again, this time less demanding and more patient. Not ordering the mana to move but simply... opening a path for it. Imagining his right arm as a channel rather than a destination.","Then something shifted.","It was faint. Barely noticeable to him. Like the first movement of air before a breeze decided what it wanted to be.","The cool pressure in his core stirred.","It moved, slowly, reluctantly.","Noah held his breath without meaning to.","’Don’t break it. Don’t even think too hard. Just let it move.’","The sensation crept down his upper arm. Slow as frost forming on glass. Past his elbow. Into his forearm.","He could feel it not as heat or pain, but as a deepening coolness. It felt like his arm was slowly sinking into cold water.","His grip tightened instinctively on the hilt, and the sensation stuttered and hesitated.","’Relax the hands.’","He loosened his grip slightly. Just enough.","The mana moved into the hilt.","And then into the blade.","It was subtle, quieter than he expected. He had imagined it would feel dramatic somehow.","Something like a surge and a rush. Something that announced itself. Instead, it felt like the sword was simply drinking from him. A slow, quiet pull he barely noticed until he paid attention to it.","The mana settled into the metal of the sword slowly over time. Just the way cold settles into a room when a window is left open.","It was a gradual process.","A bead of frost. Tiny, smaller than a raindrop, clinging to the metal tip the way a dewdrop clings to the end of a leaf in the early morning before the sun decides its fate.","One small, perfect bead of ice on a plain steel sword in an empty training chamber.","Noah stared at it.","His concentration broke completely.","The mana dissolved instantly. The ice he had formed turned into particles.","The sword was just a sword again, chipped near the base, loose grip wrap, no history.","Noah straightened up slowly. His thighs ached.","His right arm felt faintly numb from shoulder to wrist. He had been holding the stance for maybe a minute in total and had successfully channeled mana for the first time.","He stood there in the room, looking at the tip of his plain, ordinary borrowed sword.","Then he laughed, short and quiet, barely a sound at all, more breath than voice.","\"Haha! It... might be easier than I thought... but I need to train it daily.\"","One minute. One tiny bead of frost. Nothing that would impress anyone. Nothing worth mentioning to a single person alive.","But the mana had produced ice.","Not by using his ability. But he had created this purely through mana.","Then he sighed.","At the peak level of the Dormant Core. That was Dormant Core High, a person could cover their weapon with the element they had affinity with.","Noah was still not capable of doing that.","This stance worked on the same principle of using one’s element to coat their weapon.","But there was something different here.","Unlike how ice users could cover their weapon with ice and sharpen it, turning it stronger and more durable with enhanced sharpness.","Here, he could perform something more than just that. That was what made this first stance more useful.","’Also... it’s like a basic form of this art... the easiest form of this blade art, which is also important to learn the next forms.’","\"I cannot wait to see the effect of this form.\"","It had worked.","Badly, briefly, and barely. But it had worked somehow.","He rolled his neck. Settled his feet back into position. Left foot forward. Right foot back. Sword low and behind him, tip toward the ground.","Both hands on the plain, worn hilt of a sword.","He breathed in once more.","And continued his training."]},{"number":65,"title":"Chapter 65: Why Did She Beat Him?","paragraphs":["Next day.","BOOM!","A figure shot through the training facility, colliding against the nearby wall.","All the students turned their gaze toward the scene, stopping their practice and staring at it. They were students of another class.","Currently, it was a combat arts class, and it was also being taught by their head instructor, Morgana. She had already given a long lecture on the topic of combat, then asked everyone to take laps around the ground.","So, the students of Noah’s class were running around the ground. She had instructed them to run a hundred laps.","Since the huge training facility hall was open at one end and attached to the vast ground outside, everything was visible from both sides.","But Damien was an exception.","Being her disciple, she had stopped him from running laps. Instead, she personally decided to train him.","At first, Noah, who was running on the ground, felt extremely jealous of Damien.","Getting special treatment from a beauty like Morgana.","Having such an amazing woman as a master.","While he and the others were running under the blazing sunlight.","He had even muttered under his breath, \"Lucky bastard.\"","But his thoughts soon changed.","BOOM!","Because even while running, he could hear the constant sounds of explosions and heavy impacts from inside the hall.","Inside, Damien was getting beaten badly.","Noah could not tell if it was training or just torture.","He was currently on his 40th lap, already tired from running, though it was still bearable.","All this time, his eyes kept drifting toward the hall, watching Morgana beat Damien mercilessly.","Now Damien sat leaning against the wall, breathing heavily. His cheeks were bruised, and blood leaked from his broken lips.","\"Haff... haff...\" Noah was running hard. His breathing was heavy as he gasped for air. Running a hundred laps was no easy task. Sweat dripped over his body.","\"Noah Eldritch! Stop running and come here!\"","A loud, authoritative voice echoed from the hall.","Noah flinched.","’What the heck? Why is she calling me?’ Noah thought, worry creeping into his mind.","Beside him, Arisha spoke with a calm, indifferent expression, \"Hmm... it seems like you stared at her too much. Now go and pay for it.\"","Her long violet hair, tied in a high ponytail, bounced with each step as she ran.","Unlike Noah, she had likely already completed more than fifty laps and had caught up to him.","Noah clicked his tongue in irritation and muttered, \"Tch! I did not stare this time.\"","He moved away from the group of students.","Sweat clung to his skin. He was wearing a white and red t-shirt along with red pants, their training uniform.","’What could be the reason...’","Noah walked into the hall from the open side, stepping out of the harsh sunlight.","His hand ran through his snow-white hair, which was wet with sweat.","Inside, Morgana Celestine stood with her usual cold and strict expression, her arms crossed under her chest.","She was standing on the sparring platform.","Today, she was dressed more casually, dark blue tight pants that clung to her thick thighs, and a maroon long-sleeve t-shirt.","Her hair was tied in a bun.","Her sharp eyes locked onto Noah the moment he entered.","Noah straightened slightly and spoke respectfully, \"Instructor... you called me. Was there something you wanted to tell me?\"","Morgana looked at him with an unreadable expression and said coldly, \"Noah... you were looking here many times while doing laps, while I was training Damien. Want to join?\"","Noah blinked a few times, then quickly shook his head in denial. There was no desire to get trained by her. He had already seen her way of teaching, and that was enough for him to stay away from her.","With an awkward smile, he replied, \"No! There is no need for that, Instructor. I do not want to bother you. I am alright with the training I am doing currently—\"","He stopped mid-sentence.","Her voice cut through his words sharply.","\"Take out your weapon and attack me.\"","Her tone left no room for refusal. She was not going to listen.","Noah gulped down his saliva. He was already tired from running, and now she was asking for a spar.","He took out his spear from his storage ring.","With slight hesitation, he said, \"Okay...\"","Morgana looked at him calmly and said, \"Attack me with whatever you want. Whatever you have.\"","Noah stepped onto the sparring platform where she stood at the opposite end.","He exhaled slowly.","’Well... I guess there is no escaping this.’","He tightened his grip on the spear.","Mana began to flow through his body.","A faint layer of energy wrapped around the spear, strengthening its blade.","At the same time, he reinforced his legs and arms.","His stance lowered.","Then","BOOM!","With a powerful kick against the ground, Noah shot forward.","His eyes were filled with determination.","As he dashed ahead, two swords made of ice formed beside him, floating slightly behind his shoulders.","The temperature around him dropped slightly.","He thrust the spear forward with full force.","At the same moment.","[Frost Bind]","A magic circle formed as ice surged beneath Morgana’s feet, instantly freezing her legs in place.","Everything happened in a single moment.","Yet she did not move, as if it meant nothing to her.","Morgana stood there calmly.","The spear tip rushed toward her face.","And it was stopped very easily.","Between her index finger and thumb.","She held the tip of the spear effortlessly.","Noah’s eyes widened slightly. ’What the hell?’","At the same time, her free hand moved.","It was so fast that Noah could not even see it.","CRACK! CRACK!","Both ice swords shattered instantly before even reaching her.","Fragments of ice scattered across the platform.","Now there was silence as Noah remained standing there, surprised.","Noah stood there, still holding the spear, a faint smile appearing on his face.","\"Guess... that is all I could do.\"","Before he could react, she moved again.","THUD!","A punch landed straight into his gut.","\"GHH—!!\"","His body bent forward as all the air left his lungs instantly.","Pain exploded through his abdomen.","Morgana’s cold voice reached his ears.","\"Continue.\"","Noah clenched his teeth, his face twisting in pain.","He forced himself to move.","His legs trembled, but he pushed forward again.","With a grunt, he lunged at her once more.","But this time.","He did not even see it.","BOOM!","The spar continued for less than a minute.","But soon his body was sent flying across the hall.","He crashed into the wall with a heavy impact before falling to the ground.","\"Ugh...!!\"","Noah groaned in pain, his body refusing to cooperate.","Morgana watched him from a distance and turned her head away in annoyance. \"Hmph!\" She got off the platform.","Beside him, a familiar figure lay in the same condition.","Damien.","For a moment, there was silence.","Then Damien started laughing while watching Noah.","Noah gritted his teeth, irritation and anger filling him.","Why had she asked him to train with her? And even beat him so brutally? What had he done wrong that she looked so furious at him?","His jaw hurt. His left cheek was swollen from her punch.","His stomach burned in pain.","Then a sudden realization came to him.","She never trained Damien personally, at least not during academy class hours. Then why today, all of a sudden, had she decided to train him?","\"Hah... haha... hahaha!\""]},{"number":66,"title":"Chapter 66: You Will Regret It!","paragraphs":["\"Hah... haha... hahaha!\"","Noah heard laughter beside him.","Despite his bruised face and broken lips, Damien laughed while looking at Noah.","With a pained grin, he said, \"Told you... it’s not special treatment...\"","Noah lay there, staring at the ceiling, then slowly turned his head and looked at Damien with suspicion.","With narrowed eyes, he asked, \"What? Why are you looking at me like that?\" Damien said while still holding back his laughter.","Noah stared at him seriously and asked, \"You... did you tell Instructor Morgana... about what I said to you outside her office?\"","Damien’s expression returned to normal. He stopped smiling, nodded casually, scratched his cheek, and said, \"I just teased her slightly. Nothing else.\"","Noah frowned and asked, \"What tease?\"","Damien replied calmly, \"About getting a boyfriend finally. That also the same age as your disciple. A young boyfriend. You are really something else, Master... that’s what I said to her... and the next moment she became furious. But she didn’t beat me there at that time.\"","Noah clenched his fists. He could not understand the audacity of this guy.","But Damien continued.","With a casual tone, he said, \"Then she coldly asked me... who told you... and who is this new young boyfriend of mine... that I don’t have any idea about... so I told her your name.\"","Noah shook his head in irritation. Any person could tell that he was just messing around and joking. How could this guy actually believe it and even tell Morgana?","’Or was it his plan to get me beaten? But he got beaten as well.’","Damien looked at him and said plainly, \"Well, you shouldn’t have lied to me in the first place.\"","A vein bulged on Noah’s forehead.","Then he forced a smile.","\"You idiot... I didn’t lie. Of course she will be angry if you tease her like that. She acted like that so you think it was not true. After all, which master would want her disciple to know that their master is having a relationship with a young man of their age? That is why she acted like this and even beat you...\"","He continued, \"While she beat me for telling you this truth... you got that? I told you not to say this to anyone. You even promised. And you broke it so instantly.\"","Damien frowned and said firmly, \"You... you still have the guts to lie to me. Stop it, Noah.\"","Noah replied stubbornly, \"I am not lying. This is the truth.\"","Damien paused for a second, then said, \"Okay then, I will just ask her.\"","He pushed himself up and stood on his feet.","Noah’s eyes widened.","\"What? Don’t do that! We both will be in more trouble!\"","Damien gave a wide smile and said confidently, \"Then so be it. I am ready to get beaten... but I will still ask her.\"","Noah quickly said, \"Okay, okay, I accept that I was lying. Don’t you dare tell her anything now!\"","He also stood up and tried to stop him.","Damien cupped his ear mockingly and said, \"What? I cannot hear you... what are you saying? Anyway, I need to go and ask her about you... and tell her what you just said.\"","\"No! Damien, I warned you, don’t do it! It will not end well for you if you do that!\" Noah said with a panicked and aggressive tone.","But Damien was in no mood to listen.","With a challenging look, he asked, \"What can you do to me?\"","He stepped closer and continued, \"I will ask her, tell her what you said... and what can you do about it? Teach me a lesson? Fight me?\"","He looked straight into Noah’s eyes and said confidently, \"You are strong, Noah... but not enough to do anything to me.\"","Noah gritted his teeth. No matter how irritated he felt, what Damien said was true.","Still, Noah did not back down.","With a firm voice, he said loudly, \"Fine! Do whatever you want... You can tell her if you want. I will not stop you... but remember my words... you will regret it...\"","His voice drew the attention of nearby students.","A few students started murmuring.","Damien looked at him with surprise. He was just trying to tease Noah since he had lied to him. But now Noah was telling him to go and tell Morgana whatever he wanted.","Soon, Damien became more amused. He smirked and said, \"You can try it.\" He was actually enjoying this. He was wondering what Noah would do now.","Then he turned and walked toward the place where Morgana was standing, who was not paying attention to whatever was going on between the two students.","Noah remained standing there. \"Tch!\"","---","It was 4 p.m. in the afternoon.","Noah stepped out of the bus in the North District of Novaris City.","The Adventurers Guild office was situated at Meridian Avenue and Fifth Street North, one of the older commercial blocks in the North District.","Noah walked through the street. It was quite crowded.","He was wearing a white t-shirt with a black jacket over it, gray pants, and white shoes.","His hair was messy, yet the man looked very handsome.","Soon, he reached his destination.","It was a tall, seven-story building. The kind with thick stone columns and elegant old-fashioned stonework. But it had been modernized. The stone was dark grey, almost black, and the gaps between the columns had been filled with sleek black panels. It gave off a feeling of old money combined with modern power.","The windows were framed in bronze-colored metal, and the glass had a slightly blue-grey tint. Everything looked expensive but not flashy.","It looked perfect for a gold-level guild. Not too flashy, nor too old-looking.","Heavy glass doors in a brushed steel frame sat at the center of the ground floor. Above them was a thin glowing panel that showed live guild stats. Active contracts, completion rate, and the gold rank indicator, like a scoreboard that never slept.","Flanking the doors were two long planters with sharp, trimmed architectural grass instead of flowers. Two security cameras slowly swept the pavement.","The Guild Sign","Above the entrance, carved into a black panel and lit from within with a warm amber glow, was the guild emblem, a crimson flame wrapped around a sword with the words CRIMSON VALE ADVENTURES GUILD in plain, confident lettering underneath.","\"Nice!\" Noah exclaimed and walked toward the entrance.","The huge gates were guarded by two guards.","Noah entered inside.","The automatic glass doors opened before he reached them. The lobby hit him immediately.","The temperature was low inside. Cool and perfect.","\"Let’s join the guild.\""]},{"number":67,"title":"Chapter 67: Adventurer’s Guild (1)","paragraphs":["The lobby was cool and quiet compared to the busy street outside.","Noah stepped in and looked around. The floor was polished concrete. The ceiling was high. To the left were some leather sofas. Straight ahead was the reception counter, long and dark, with a few staff members standing behind it.","He walked toward the counter.","One of the staff members stepped forward. She was a woman in her late twenties, wearing the guild’s grey uniform with the Crimson Vale emblem stitched in red at the collar. Her posture was straight and professional.","Her brown hair tied in neat bun.","\"Welcome to Crimson Vale,\" she said with a polite smile. \"How can I help you?\"","Noah looked at her for a moment. She was pretty in a neat. The kind of person who had probably answered that same question a thousand times and still made it sound genuine. Professional and patience.","\"Hello my name is Noah, I want to join the guild,\" he said.","\"Of course.\" She picked up a tablet. \"May I ask your current status? Student, independent, or referred?\"","\"Student,\" Noah said. He reached into his storage ring and pulled out a small card. \"Novaris Academy. First year.\"","He placed the ID on the counter and slid it toward her.","She picked it up and looked it over carefully, tapping the details into her tablet.","She paused for a moment after reading his surname. After all there was only one Eldritch family in whole empire. One of the dukedom.","But she didn’t react. Years of work experience has made her act perfectly.","\"Novaris Academy,\" she said, nodding slightly. \"Good. That will speed things up.\" She set the ID down and reached under the counter, placing a smooth crystal sphere on the surface between them. It was about the size of a fist, perfectly clear.","\"Before registration, we need to do a quick assessment,\" she said. \"Standard procedure. Could you tell me your core level first?\"","\"Dormant core,\" Noah said. \"High rank.\"","She made a note. \"I’ll need to confirm that. Please place your hand on the sphere and channel your mana into it. Just a steady flow, nothing forced.\"","Noah looked at the sphere for a second, then placed his hand on it.","He pushed his mana in slowly.","The sphere began to glow.","The color that bled through was black, deep and dark, like ink spreading through water. But at the edges, where the light was thinnest, there was something else. A faint trace of bronze. Subtle, but there. It curled at the rim of the glow like the last breath of a flame.","The woman watched it closely. Her expression stayed professional but her eyes lingered on it for just a moment longer than usual.","She made another note on her tablet.","\"Dormant core, peak level,\" she said. \"Confirmed.\"","She set the tablet down and looked at him. \"Because you’re a registered Academy student, your application gets processed under the fast track. You won’t need to wait for a panel review.\" She gave him a small nod. \"Please take a seat over there. It won’t be long.\"","Noah glanced toward the left side of the lobby. There was a row of dark leather sofas in the corner, a low table between them with some guild brochures fanned out on top. He walked over and dropped into one of the seats, leaning back and resting his arm along the side.","He looked up at the ceiling for a while.","A few other people were sitting nearby. A pair of adventurers in light gear talking quietly between themselves. An older man filling out a form with a pen, old-fashioned about it.","At one wall a huge screean was attached to it. Many adventures stand near it.","Various mission presented on it. For adventurers to choose them.","Most normal quest or say missions were bringing specific monster’s dead bodies.","Few mission about monster cores.","Noah closed his eyes for a moment, letting the guild’s unspoken rules settle in his mind.","The Adventurer’s Guild wasn’t just a place to find work. It was a system. Monsters roamed the wilds and nested deep within forests.","And it was adventurers who kept that threat in check. In return, whatever they killed was theirs. The body, the core, everything.","They could sell the carcass to the guild for quick Zela, keep the mana core for their own cultivation, or take their loot elsewhere entirely. The guild had no claim over a free hunt.","But dungeons were different.","Every dungeon,forest area and labyrinth operating under guild jurisdiction was guild territory.","Any adventurer who raided those depths did so under guilds permission. A fixed percentage of all loot collected inside had to be handed over to the guild, no exceptions. It wasn’t negotiable and it wasn’t optional. That was the cost of raiding under their banner.","Outside of hunting, the guild board handled everything else. Nobles, merchants, wealthy people, anyone with Zela and a problem could register a mission at the guild. Even villages and commuinities with some problems also register mission.","Monster exterminations, material collection, escort requests, dungeon clearances. The guild verified the reward, held it in escrow, and matched the job to an adventurer of appropriate rank. Clean and simple. While taking commision from it.","Noah opened his eyes.","It didn’t take long. Maybe ten minutes.","\"Mr. Noah?\"","He opened his eyes. The woman from the counter was standing a few feet away, holding a small card.","He got up and followed her back to the counter.","\"Your registration is complete,\" she said, placing the card on the surface and turning it to face him.","He picked it up.","It was slim and firm, with a dark grey background. His photo was printed cleanly in the top left corner. Beside it, his name, his age, and his core level. Dormant Core, high. At the bottom right, his rank was printed in clear lettering.","F+","Below the rank was the Crimson Vale emblem, small but sharp.","\"This is your official adventurer’s guild card,\" she said. \"Keep it on you whenever you’re taking on contracts or entering guild facilities. It’s your identification within the system.\"","\"Got it.\" Noah slipped the card into his jacket pocket. \"Thanks.\"","\"Is there anything else I can help you with?\"","He thought for a second.","\"Yeah, actually.\" He leaned slightly against the counter. \"Can I buy monsters mana cores here? Do you sell those?\"","She nodded. \"Yes, we do. The trading window is just down that corridor on the right. They handle core purchases, sales, and exchanges.\"","\"Perfect.\" Noah straightened up and gave her a small smile. \"Appreciate it.\"","She returned the smile, brief and polite.","Noah picked up his bag from the floor, glanced once more at the guild card in his pocket, and turned toward the corridor.","F+ rank.","He looked at it again for just a second before pocketing it.","It was a start."]},{"number":68,"title":"Chapter 68: Adventurer’s Guild (2)","paragraphs":["Noah followed the corridor to the right.","It was shorter than he expected. Maybe thirty steps and he was there.","The trading window was a wide open room connected to the main corridor through a broad archway. It was simpler than the lobby. No polished floors or high ceilings here.","Just plain walls, bright overhead lighting, and a long counter running across the far side of the room divided into several sections, each one its own window.","A few men stood behind the counter, each handling their own section. Some were busy with customers. A couple were sorting through small containers lined up behind them on shelves, each one labeled and organized by rank.","Noah scanned the room.","One of the windows had just freed up. A man was walking away from it, tucking something into his coat pocket. Noah moved over before anyone else did.","The staff member behind that window was an ordinary-looking man. Middle-aged, square jaw, nothing particularly remarkable about him. He was not unfriendly. Or he wasn’t warm either. He was just there, doing his job like normal person.","He looked up as Noah approached.","\"What can I do for you, Sir?\"","\"I’m looking to buy some monster mana cores,\" Noah said. \"Mind if I ask about the prices first?\"","\"Go ahead.\"","Noah put both hands on the edge of the counter.","Here was the thing about mana cores. Every monster had one. When a monster died, the core it left behind still held mana inside it was compressed, raw, and dense.","For mana core awakened people at the lower levels, absorbing that mana was one of the most practical ways to push their own core forward.","One didn’t need to train for hours in a mana-thin room. They just needed a core, a quiet space, and enough focus to pull the energy in and cycle it through one’s own.","Though it also time consuming. But its better than normal meditation and absorbing mana from surrounding. It faster than that.","The problem was compatibility.","If the core’s mana density was too low, your body would absorb it and barely feel a thing. Waste of money. If it was too high, it risked destabilizing one’s own core trying to process it. Also a problem, but a much more painful one.","Noah was at Dormant Core, high grade. That put him right at the bottom edge of actually being useful to himself. F rank monster cores, the lowest tier were simply too weak.","The mana packed into an F rank core was thin and scattered. Absorbing one would be like trying to fill a bucket with a damp cloth. Technically something went in, but not enough to matter.","E rank cores were different.","\"E rank cores,\" Noah said. \"What’s the price on E-, E, and E+?\"","The man reached under the counter and pulled out a tab, sliding it across. Price were written on them.","Noah looked it over.","’E− Core — 50,000 nova points/Zela’","The weakest of the E rank tier. Mana density was low but stable. Good for someone just crossing out of the F range, but for Noah at peak Dormant, they would work. Not efficiently, but they would work. One would need a lot of them.","E Core — 1,00,000 nova points/Zela","Standard E rank. Solid mana density. The kind most lower-level cultivators worked with when they had a proper budget. One of these was worth about two E minus cores in terms of actual usable mana, and the absorption was cleaner.","’E+ Core — 2,00,000 nova points/Zela’","The top of the E rank tier. Dense, concentrated mana. Much better yield per core. These were what serious mana users at his level actually wanted. One E plus core could do the work of two or three standard E cores if absorbed properly.","Noah studied the numbers quietly.","His budget was 500,000 nova. He had gotten them as reward. In Novaris city, nova points and zela were the same thing in practice. One to one, used interchangeably depending on whether a person were dealing with a guild system or a private seller.","500,000 nova sounded like a lot until you were standing in front of a trading window.","\"What about D rank?\" Noah asked. \"Just so I know.\"","The man tapped a line further down on the sheet.","D− Core — 3,00,000 nova points/zela","D Core — 4,50,000 nova points/zela","D+ Core — 6,00,000 nova points/zela","Noah stared at those numbers for a second.","A single D rank core cost nearly all his entire budget. A D+ cross his budget, everything he had, for one core. One. And while D rank mana would have been significantly more powerful for his core, the gap in price was simply not realistic right now.","He exhaled quietly through his nose.","D rank was out. That was just the reality of it.","He looked back at the E rank section and did the math quickly in his head.","E plus cores were the best value if he wanted quality. At 200000 nova each, his 500,000 would get him two cores with a little left over. That was decent.","He made his decision.","\"I’ll two standard E+ rank cores,\" he said. \"Thirty of them.\"","The man nodded without any particular reaction. He turned to the shelves behind him and began pulling out a container, opening it to reveal rows of small cores lined up inside. Each one was about the size of a tennis ball, slightly translucent, with a faint inner glow that pulsed slowly like a dim heartbeat.","\"Two E+ rank cores,\" the man said, counting them out into a separate carry case. \"That comes to 4,00,000 nova points or zela.\"","Noah took out his mobile and send 4,00,000 nova points in one go.","The man processed it, slid the case across, and handed Noah a small receipt.","\"Anything else?\"","Noah picked up the case and looked at the cores through the transparent lid for a moment. Thirty of them, sitting there quietly.","\"No,\" he said. \"That’s everything.\"","He tucked the case into his storage ring, folded the receipt, and turned to leave.","Two E+ rank cores.","It wasn’t much. But it was enough to get started.","’With this I can brokethrough. Also I can try taking some mission or visit dungeon once I brokethrough awakened core rank.’"]},{"number":69,"title":"Chapter 69: Absorbing mana","paragraphs":["The dormitory was quiet.","It was late evening by the time Noah got back. The living room was empty. Lights on ceiling were on, throwing a warm low light across the room.","Noah took of his jacket and threw it on couch.","He took out the carry case from his storage ring, opened it, and looked at what was inside.","Two cores.","That was all he had managed to get. Two E+ cores. Not thirty. Not even close to thirty. The E+ cores were better quality than the standard ones, denser and cleaner, but they had cost him 2,00,000 nova points each. With his budget already stretched from other expenses, two was what he could afford without leaving himself completely empty.","He picked one up. It sat in his palm, small and smooth, slightly warm to the touch. The faint glow inside it pulsed slowly. Almost like breathing. It was siz3 of tennis ball.","He set the case aside, moved the coffee table out of the way, and sat down on the floor in the middle of the room.","\"Time to absorb it\" he muttered with smile.","He sat cross-legged. Back straight. Hands resting on his knees, palms facing up.","The core sat in his lap. He closed his eyes.","---","The first thing he did was slow his breathing down.","He let the noise of the building fade out. The distant sound of someone walking upstairs. A door closing somewhere the hall.","All of it drifted back until it was just background. Until there was nothing in front of him but the darkness behind his eyes and the faint warmth of the core in his lap.","Then he reached.","It was something quieter than that. He turned his focus inward, the way he had been taught at the Academy and at his family. When he was not exiled. He extended his awareness outward just slightly, toward the core.","He felt it immediately.","The mana inside the core was raw. That was the only word for it. It wasn’t clean or smooth the way the mana in the Academy’s training rooms felt.","This was wild mana, the kind that had lived inside a monster, shaped by its nature and its instincts. It had texture to it. A kind of pressure. Like putting your hand near a fire and feeling the heat before the flame.","Noah began to draw it in slowly.","Not all at once. That was the mistake beginners made, pulling too hard and flooding themselves with more than they could handle.","He drew it in like pulling a thread. Seady and controlled. A thin stream of mana lifting out of the core and flowing into him through his palms.","It entered his body and immediately the work began.","Raw mana was not something you could just push straight to your core. It didn’t work that way.","Monster mana carried impurities in it. Traces of the creature it came from. Fragments of foreign energy that didn’t belong in a human core system.","If one let those impurities travel through unchecked and pushed them into the core, that would damage it. Slowly at first. Then seriously.","So they had to clean it first.","As the mana flowed in through his hands, Noah directed it upward through his arms, into his chest, and began circulating it through his body.","A slow loop. Arms, chest, back, down through his legs, back up again. Round and round, like running water through a filter.","With each pass, he caught the impurities.","It required focus. The impurities didn’t announce themselves. They were subtle, little knots and rough edges in the flow of energy.","He had to feel for them as the mana moved through him, catch them, and push them out. Through his skin, through his breath, out of his body entirely.","It was slow work.","The mana that came out the other side of that process was thinner. There was less of it.","He gathered that purified mana carefully and began guiding it downward.","The lower dantian.","It sat deep in his abdomen, a few inches below his navel, in the place where it had always known as the centre of the body’s energy. That was where the core lived.","Noah’s core was black.","Dormant cores presented. Pure black, like a piece of polished obsidian sitting in the middle of him. It was small still. Compressed into itself the way a Dormant core was before it had enough energy to crack open and move into the next stage.","He brought the purified mana down to it.","The mana touched the surface of his core and began to settle against it, thin as a coat of paint at first, layering over the black surface slowly.","Some of it was absorbed directly into the core, drawn in through the surface and adding to its density from the inside. The rest pressed against the outside, compressing, adding weight and pressure to the shell.","Both mattered.","The mana absorbed inside added to the core’s overall energy. The mana compressing on the outside added to its density and solidity, slowly building the pressure that would eventually be needed to push the core past its current stage.","It was like filling a container while simultaneously making the container stronger.","Noah held his focus on it and kept the flow steady.","After a while, the core in his lap began to feel lighter.","Sweat dripped over his face.","The mana coming off it had thinned slightly, the way a candle dims a little as the wax lowers. The core had given up what it could for now. The rest was locked inside it still, and it would take more time to absorbed it.","That was the other thing about monster cores.","One could not drain one in a single sitting. The mana inside was compressed too tightly. It released in layers, slowly, over multiple sessions.","One core at this level would take him several days of consistent meditation to fully absorb. Rushing it did nothing. The mana simply wouldn’t come out any faster than it was willing to.","Noah didn’t rush it.","He held the circulation going for another hour, gathering every trace of clean mana he could pull through, layering it carefully over his core, and releasing the impurities with each slow breath out.","When the flow became too thin to work with efficiently, he stopped.","After hours of circulating and absorbed mana.","He opened his eyes.","The room was the same as he had left it. The core in his lap had lost a little of its glow, slightly dimmer than before, but still pulsing faintly. Still plenty left in it.","Noah exhaled and rolled his neck slowly.","His body felt warm. It was uncomfortable. The kind of warmth that came from the inside, like he had been sitting in mild sunlight for an hour.","His core felt marginally heavier than before. It was slightly denser. Not much different compare to before. But he could tell that he had some progress.","But he noticed.","He picked up the core and held it in front of his face for a moment, looking at the dim pulse inside it.","A few more days of this. Then the second one.","Two cores total. That was what he had.","It wasn’t much. But right now, it was everything he could work with.","He placed it carefully back in the case, closed the lid, and stored it in his ring. Then he got up off the floor, moved the coffee table back into place, and went to get a glass of water from the kitchen.","Two E+ cores.","He would make every bit of them count.","\"This much is enough for today.\"","He muttered while his body was sweat drenched. Then he opened his status.","===STATUS===","Name: Noah Eldritch","Race: Human","Age: 19 years","Strength: 90","Speed: 76","Stamina: 93","Endurance: 73","Charm: 510","Mana: 834","Core Rank: Dormant (High)","Potential: Refined Core (High)","Profession: [Combatant Lvl.1]","Technique: [Frozen Lotus Blade Art]>","Affinity: Ice","Spells: [Ice Shard], [Frost Bind]","Innate Ability: Ice Creation","===","\"In a week...I can broke through.\" He said with small smile."]},{"number":70,"title":"Chapter 70: Weapon Art","paragraphs":["Few days later.","Currently, it was Weapon Art class.","All the students were once again standing inside the huge training facility. At this point, Noah had become familiar with this place.","And the instructor appointed for this class was none other than Victor Hale.","He stood in front of them, a dirt-blonde-haired man. He was around six feet tall with a well-built physique, wearing a black suit.","His sharp green eyes scanned the students, his face strict and composed.","He was one of the strongest heroes in the human empire. As strong as Morgana.","He was known for his mastery over multiple weapons.","A man from a commoner background, who had risen to become one of the fiercest figures in the world.","Noah had heard many things about him. How he could use multiple weapons effortlessly.","Victor stood with his hands behind his back.","His gaze swept across the entire class before he finally spoke.","His voice was calm, yet carried a natural authority.","\"Weapon Arts are not just techniques.\"","The hall fell silent instantly.","\"You all have weapons. Some of you swing them. Some of you stab. Some of you rely on brute strength. Some on speed.\"","He paused, his eyes narrowing slightly.","\"But none of that matters if you do not understand your weapon.\"","He began walking slowly in front of them.","\"The difference between a beginner and a true combatant is not talent. It is understanding.\"","He stopped. Then continued, \"A sword is not just for cutting. A spear is not just for thrusting. A bow is not just for shooting arrows.\"","His gaze hardened.","\"A weapon is an extension of your body. And your body is an extension of your intent.\"","Some students unconsciously straightened their posture.","Victor continued.","\"A martial manual is not just a set of instructions. It is the experience of someone who has already walked the path you are trying to walk.\"","He raised one finger. \"It teaches you efficiency.\"","Another finger. \"It teaches you control. And most importantly... it teaches you how to survive.\"","His eyes moved across the class again. \"Many of you think power comes from strength or mana.\"","He shook his head slightly. \"Power comes from application.\"","He turned and pointed toward the weapon racks placed at the side of the hall.","\"A weak strike at the right time is more deadly than a powerful strike at the wrong time.\"","Silence filled the hall.","Even Noah was listening seriously now.","Victor crossed his arms. \"For bow users... your weapon is not just your hands.\"","\"You must understand distance. Wind. Timing. Movement.\"","\"A single arrow... if used correctly... can decide the outcome of a battle before it even begins.\"","He shifted his gaze.","\"For close combat users... positioning matters more than strength.\"","\"You step wrong once... and you die.\"","A cold chill ran through some of the students.","Victor’s voice remained steady. \"You will learn many things in this academy. Spells, techniques, and theory.\"","\"But without proper weapon mastery... all of it is meaningless in real combat.\"","He let those words sink in. Then, after a brief pause, his tone changed slightly. \"Now.\"","He turned fully toward the class. \"I will be assigning each of you a martial art manual.\"","Murmurs spread instantly.","Victor raised his hand. \"Silence.\"","The murmurs stopped immediately. \"This is not optional.\"","His voice turned firm. \"It is compulsory to learn the martial art I give you.\"","\"If you already possess a strong manual for your main weapon... then you will receive one for your secondary weapon.\"","He looked at them one by one. \"I do not care about your status. Noble or commoner. Talent or no talent.\"","\"I will decide what suits you.\" Then he called out the first name.","\"Damien Ashworth.\"","Damien stepped forward calmly.","Victor looked at him for a moment.","\"Primary weapon?\"","\"Sword.\"","\"Secondary?\"","\"None.\"","Victor nodded slightly. \"You already possess a strong sword foundation.\"","He extended his hand. A faint glow appeared, and a manual materialized. \"You will take this.\"","Damien received it.","\"[Twin Edge Flow]. A dual-blade combat style. You will begin learning it. Dual short swords. It will be easy since you only have one profession.\"","Damien nodded. \"Yes, Instructor.\"","\"Next. Kaelan Nighfall.\"","Just like that, names were called.","Victor’s gaze shifted as it was Noah’s turn.","\"Noah Eldritch.\"","Noah stepped forward. Victor looked at him for a longer time than others.","His sharp green eyes seemed to analyze everything.","\"What profession? I mean, which weapon you use as primary weapon among them.\"","After thinking for a moment, Noah decided to lie.","\"Spear. And I have a very good weapon art for it.\"","\"Hmm... Secondary?\"","Noah paused slightly. \"...bow.\"","Victor’s gaze sharpened slightly. He observed Noah for a while. \"Okay. Take this one.\"","He pulled out a manual from his storage ring and handed it to Noah.","Noah took it and looked at the name.","[Flowing String Archery]","\"Yes, Instructor. Thank you for this.\"","He bowed to him slightly as a gesture of gratitude.","Victor looked at him one last time before speaking.","\"Do not waste it.\"","Noah gave a slight nod.","Then Noah went back, while Victor continued distributing. After completing it, Victor stepped back and looked at the entire class.","\"You all have one week.\"","His voice turned cold again. \"Show me results.\"","Silence filled the hall once more. The real training had just begun.","--","\"Alright! Now it’s time to try something new.\"","Currently, Noah was holding a bow in his hand.","Yes, a bow.","The reason why he told Victor that he uses a bow as a secondary weapon was simple.","He had gotten a new profession called Combatant.","Where he could use most weapons at a basic level.","As his profession level increased, his proficiency would increase.","The manual art he had gotten worked on all weapons that had a blade. So getting a manual for a spear, sword, or any other weapon having a blade was not worth it.","So he chose a weapon on which his Frozen Lotus Blade Art was not usable.","\"It’s my first time trying to use a bow. Let’s practice first and then try to learn my new martial art manual.\""]},{"number":71,"title":"Chapter 71: Archery (1)","paragraphs":["The Academy’s training facility was large.","It was split into different sections depending on what you were working on. Strength training in one wing. Sparring platforms in another. And further back, past a set of double doors, was the ranged practice area in one corner of the training hall.","Noah pushed through the doors and stepped inside.","The shooting range was long and narrow. High ceiling. The walls on either side were lined with thick padding.","Downrange, at various distances, were practice targets. Simple circular designs, rings getting smaller toward the center. Some were stationary. A few of the far ones moved slowly on a track, sliding left and right at a low pace.","A handful of students were already there. One girl near the front was practicing with a short bow, loosing arrows in a steady rhythm. Two boys further down were arguing quietly over something, one of them holding a crossbow. Nobody paid Noah any attention when he walked in.","He went to the equipment rack along the side wall.","The practice bows were plain and simple. Wooden, medium draw weight, nothing fancy. Designed for beginners. He picked one up and turned it over in his hands. It was lighter than he expected. Smooth grain. The string was taut but not extremely tight.","He grabbed a quiver of practice arrows from the rack beside it and slung it over his shoulder.","He walked to an open lane and stood facing the nearest target. Standard distance. Not too far.","He looked at the bow.","Noah had the Combatant profession.","In simple terms, it meant he wouldn’t look completely lost.","But basic proficiency was still just that. Basic. It gave him the form. It didn’t give him the repetition, the muscle memory, or the feel that only came from actual practice.","He nocked an arrow on the string.","His fingers found the string naturally enough. Middle finger above the arrow, ring finger below, index finger light on top. His left arm extended, holding the bow out toward the target. He pulled the string back slowly.","The draw resistance pushed against him. It was not overwhelming, but present. He felt it in his shoulder and across his upper back.","He lined up the arrow with the target. His gaze fixed on the target. He observed it for a while.","Then let half of it out. The arrow flew.","It hit the outer ring of the target. It didn’t hit the edge or outermost part, but not close to the center either.","Noah lowered the bow and looked at where it had landed.","\"Not bad for a first try,\" Noah said with a satisfied smile.","The Combatant profession had given him the basic form. His elbow had been in roughly the right position. His grip had been decent. But his aim was off, and he could feel that his release hadn’t been clean.","\"I should try more.\"","He nocked another arrow. And shot again.","He spent the next hour at the range.","He didn’t rush through the arrows. He took each shot slowly. Drew, lined up, checked his breathing, released. Then he walked downrange, pulled his arrows out of the target, walked back, and did it again.","By the third round, his shots were grouping better. Still outer ring, mostly. But they were landing closer together, which told him his form was becoming more consistent even if his aim still needed work.","His shoulder started aching around the forty-minute mark. The draw was repetitive and his body wasn’t used to it yet. He shook his arm out, rested for a few minutes, then kept going.","\"Okay... that much is enough. Let’s rest for a while.\"","Noah went toward the bench and sat, taking out a bottle from his storage ring. He drank the cool water.","He pulled out the manual for archery, given by Professor Victor.","[Flowing String Archery]","It was a weapon art of 2.5 star. It was not too good nor bad. Rather, it was mid. But very useful for learning. It’s easy, and won’t take much time, so one can focus on their primary weapon art.","He studied it and read the first form.","\"A 2.5-star manual...\"","His lips curved slightly.","\"It’s not amazing... but not bad either.\"","For someone else, it might have been average. But for Noah, it was perfect. Something simple and easy. Something he could learn quickly. Something that wouldn’t interfere with his blade art.","He flipped it open. His eyes moved across the first page.","Then the next. And then he read the first form of this art.","Form I — Still Calm Strike.","Noah’s posture straightened slightly as he began reading carefully.","His eyes scanned every word. He read every instruction. Every explanation.","As the name suggested, it was an art that depended on flow. Such as the flow of water.","\"...a completely calm body produces a completely deadly shot...\"","\"...circulate mana in a slow, even current...\"","\"...do not force it...\"","\"...guide it...\"","His brows furrowed slightly. A thoughtful expression appeared on his face.","\"Calm, even flow and no forcing.\"","It sounded simple. But it wasn’t that simple.","Noah had already experienced something similar while practicing the Frozen Lotus stance.","Controlling mana without forcing it. While doing that, he needed to be as calm as possible.","Letting it move naturally. That wasn’t something that came easily. But he had trained it before.","His fingers tapped lightly against the page as he continued reading.","\"...fix your aim on a precise point... release only when the mana feels settled...\"","He closed the manual slowly. A quiet exhale left his lips.","\"...So, it’s about shooting right.\"","He leaned forward, resting his elbows on his knees. His gaze drifted toward the targets downrange.","\"Let’s practice the first form. No need to waste time.\"","Then he stood up. His expression had changed again.","He was more calm and focused.","\"Alright... let’s try this properly.\"","Noah walked back toward the shooting lane. He picked up the bow again. The familiar weight settled into his hand.","He reached back and pulled out an arrow from the quiver.","He nocked it as the arrow slid into place. He raised the bow. The tip of the arrow directed at the target.","But this time, he didn’t draw immediately.","He paused, his feet adjusted slightly. Shoulder-width apart. Right foot half a step back. Just like the manual instructed.","He started to learned the first form."]},{"number":72,"title":"Chapter 72: Archery (2)","paragraphs":["He inhaled slowly, then exhaled. His eyes closed for a brief second. \"...circulate mana in a slow, even current...\"","Noah focused inward. He could feel his mana. Resting within him, deep inside his core.","His mana was calm inside, with some coldness to it. He didn’t try to force it. Didn’t push it toward the bow.","\"Try to guide it slowly and naturally. Just like how water flows in one direction inside a river. Without anything to force it. Let it move.\"","Through his body, from his core, through his chest, down his arm. The sensation was faint.","But it was there.","His eyes opened. He raised the bow again.","Then he drew. The string stretched back. The resistance pressed against his muscles. But this time, his focus wasn’t on strength.","It was on flow. The mana moved down his arm into the arrow.","It was just flowing.","His breathing slowed. Keeping his body still and calm. His gaze locked onto the target.","Not the whole target.","But on a point. A single ring and a single spot.","\"...wait until it settles.\"","He held the arrow. He let the mana cover the arrow like water filling an empty cup. He just showed his will, and mana naturally listened to him without resistance. Without any force from him.","Seconds passed. The world around him faded. The faint sounds of other students.","The air shifted. Even the ache in his shoulder—all of it dulled.","There was only him, his bow and arrow, and his target.","Finally, he released the arrow. The string snapped forward. The arrow flew as a clean sound cut through the air. A straight blue line formed in the air in the direction of the target.","It didn’t waver because of the air. It cut through in the same line, same direction. It cut through the deviation.","Thud.","But closer to the center than before.","Noah’s eyes narrowed slightly.","\"...I felt it.\"","It was different. The shot felt a lot more stable.","It felt as if the arrow moved as he wanted. It was controlled. Yet he didn’t force it.","The tip of the arrow had torn into the target more than half of it.","A smile came to his face.","\"One more time.\"","He nocked another arrow. He didn’t rush. He repeated everything.","He repeated everything again and again. Sweat dripped down his forehead. But he didn’t stop. It was the last class, so he didn’t need to worry.","Time passed. Minutes turned into an hour. Then more.","At first, his mana control kept breaking.","Sometimes it wouldn’t flow at all. Sometimes it scattered halfway through the draw. Sometimes his concentration broke just before release.","He tried again.","His arms grew heavier. His shoulders burned more than before. Not just from drawing, but from holding. His breathing grew rough at times. His grip slipped once or twice. His fingers trembled.","He continued.","\"...Don’t force it...\"","\"...let it flow...\"","He repeated those words in his mind. Over and over. Like a rhythm. Like a guide.","Slowly, and very slowly, something began to change.","The mana flow became smoother. Less resistance. Less interruption.","The draw felt... cleaner. The release became sharper and more natural.","Thud.","Thud.","Thud.","His arrows began grouping tighter. Closer to the center.","Not perfect, but no longer scattered.","Another hour passed.","Finally, Noah lowered the bow. His arm dropped slightly.","A tired breath escaped his lips.","\"Haaah... dammit! I overdid it.\"","His fingers loosened around the string. His shoulders slumped just a little. Sweat dripped down the side of his face.","His chest rose and fell steadily. He stood there for a moment.","Looking at the target.","A small cluster of arrows. Not dead center.","They were not at the center, but for the first time, it was a lot better.","He exhaled slowly.","\"...Yeah.\"","A faint smile appeared on his face.","\"It’s working.\"","It was working.","He turned and walked back toward the bench again. His steps were slower this time.","He sat down. Leaning back slightly.","There was a quiet sense of progress.","He closed his eyes for a moment.","\"...Just the first form...\"","\"Status.\"","---","===STATUS===","Name: Noah Eldritch","Race: Human","Age: 19 years","Strength: 90","Speed: 76","Stamina: 93","Endurance: 73","Charm: 510","Mana: 834","Core Rank: Dormant (High)","Potential: Refined Core (High)","Profession: [Combatant Lvl.1]","Technique: [Frozen Lotus Blade Art]>, [Flowing String Archery]>","Affinity: Ice","Spells: [Ice Shard], [Frost Bind]","Innate Ability: Ice Creation","---","He clicked on the technique. As it showed his progression.","---","===","[Frozen Lotus Blade Art]>","[First Petal: Dewdrop Stance] >>> (Proficiency: 6%)","[Flowing String Archery]>","[First Form - Still Calm Strike] >>> (Proficiency: 9%)","===","---","\"Only 6% for blade... well, it’s hard and a five-star weapon art, and 9% for archery—it’s good considering I barely started...\"","A small breath left his lips.","At this rate, he needed to train a lot of hours daily if he wanted to progress.","---","While Noah was practicing till the evening.","In one corner of academy few students were having some important discussion.","In a on quite place behind the dormitory building.","Five men were having discussion about upcoming VR match.","The battles which were postponed would be taken after two weeks. On Saturday of third week after current one.","Amon the five people three were Edward, Testu and Richard","The idiot trio who fought against Noah.","With them were other two men. A young man with six feet hight. Curly black hair. Slightly tan skin. Amber eyes.","The young man spoke to another man beside him. \"Michael what’s your thought on incoming battle.\"","Michael who was nearly six feet. Having dark green hair with emerald eyes replied. \"Travis. For me it was just practice match...but man they turned it into unit test. Now it’s important. We have to win for getting good marks.\"","\"But we got some problems. Don’t you think?\" Travis asked with raised brow.","Edward spoke this time. \"Of course. Our opponent is class A-1. The class who have both rank 1 and rank 2 students of first year.\"","\"So what? Our class also have Travis. Just because he is third rank doesn’t mean they are better than him.\" Testu used his index finger to pushed them like a smart guy.","\"But it’s clear...they are too strong. Our chances of winning is low. Damn it’s not like they put all strong students in one class. We have rank 3 and 6...and more...but it’s still feels insignificant.\" Michael said while rubbing his chin.","Travis was silent. Thinking about something very deeply. \"Edward, any scum student you know from A-1? Who can be bought and betray their class.\"","His expression turned serious. \"I cannot let go this chance I need to get more points. So I can achieve first rank this semester.\""]},{"number":73,"title":"Chapter 73: Breakthrough","paragraphs":["In his dormitory room, Noah was absorbing mana from the core once again.","It had been more than a week since he first started using monster cores to absorb mana.","Sweat dripped down his face from hours of meditation. His snow-white hair clung to his forehead, damp and heavy. His white t-shirt stuck to his skin.","He sat cross-legged with his hands resting on his knees and his back straight, breathing heavily from the effort of meditating for so long.","He had not gone to training today.","He was too close to let anything interrupt it.","For the past week he had been completely focused. The moment classes ended each day, he would head straight to the training hall.","Stretching first, then weapon practice, working through both his bow and blade arts until his arms were sore. After that he would sit down and absorb mana from the cores, cycling it through his body late into the night.","He had also spent time learning his new spell, Snow Mist, in between sessions. That had taken him less than a week to fully grasp. His proficiency with both weapon arts had grown steadily as well, improving a little more with each day of drilling.","But today was different.","Today, he was not training. He was finishing something.","The raw mana circulated through his entire body in slow, wide loops. As it moved, he filtered it carefully, pushing the impurities out with each pass until what remained was clean and smooth. That purified mana then moved downward, toward his core.","The core was full.","It had been filling gradually over the past week, mana layering over its surface and pressing into it session by session. Now it had reached its absolute limit. There was no more room inside it and no more room around it. It had taken everything it could take.","It was time.","Noah wrapped the remaining pure mana around the outside of his black core and began to compress it. Layer after layer pressing inward, tightening, squeezing the core from every direction at once.","His breathing became ragged. His heart beat faster. His blood felt hot as it moved through him.","He kept pressing.","More. Tighter. He pushed the compression as far as it would go, holding it at the limit until the strain ran through every part of him.","Then came the sound.","A sharp crack from somewhere deep inside his body.","The mana layered over the core began to glow. A bright blue light bloomed in his lower abdomen, and the same faint blue radiance spread outward, bleeding softly through his skin until his whole body was lit with a quiet azure glow.","The surface of the core began to fracture. Fine lines spreading outward from the centre, branching and crossing like ice breaking under pressure.","’Just a little more.’","He gathered every last trace of mana he had and drove it into the core.","CRACK!!","The fractures split wide.","BOOM","A shockwave rolled outward from his body, silent but physical, pressing against the walls of the room.","The core that had once been black was black no longer.","It was bronze.","The azure glow faded from his skin slowly, like a light being turned down. On his lap, the empty monster core sat dull and colorless, completely spent. Every last trace of mana drained out of it.","His eyelids fluttered. He opened his eyes slowly.","A smile spread across his face.","\"Hah... haah...\" He exhaled hard, chest heaving. \"Finally. I broke through into Awakened Core, low stage.\"","He sat with it for a moment, just breathing.","Then, quietly. \"Status.\"","His status window opened in front of him.","===STATUS===","Name: Noah Eldritch","Race: Human","Age: 19 years","Strength: 108","Speed: 98","Stamina: 105","Endurance: 90","Charm: 556","Mana: 1048","Core Rank: Awakened (low)","Potential: Refined Core (High)","Profession: [Combatant Lvl.1]","Technique: [Frozen Lotus Blade Art]>, [Flowing String Archery]>","Affinity: Ice","Spells: [Ice Shard], [Frost Bind],[Snow Mist]","Innate Ability: Ice Creation","---","He stared at it for a moment.","Then he laughed.","\"Hahaha! Finally some progress! I actually did it!\"","He let himself fall backward, his back hitting the floor with a soft thud. He lay there, staring up at the ceiling with a wide grin on his face, breathing slowly as the tension drained out of his body.","After a while the grin faded into something quieter.","\"But I can’t stop here.\" He spoke to the ceiling, his voice low and even. \"I need to get stronger. A lot stronger. Before whatever comes next. Which I still have no idea about.\"","He thought about his potential rank. Refined Core, High Grade. It was decent. But decent was not enough for what he suspected was coming. He needed a way to push past that limit. Break the ceiling on his potential entirely if he could.","’I just need to find something that can do that.’","He turned his head and looked at the clock on the wall.","5:30 in the evening.","He sat up slowly, rolled his neck, and exhaled.","\"Alright. That’s enough for today. I’ll take the night off.\"","He got up and went to the bathroom for a long, warm shower. He stayed in longer than he needed to, letting the heat work through his shoulders and back.","When he stepped out, he changed into casual clothes and stood in front of the mirror.","He looked at his reflection for a moment.","Then his expression shifted into something amused.","\"Hmm.\" He tilted his head slightly. \"I think I actually look better after the breakthrough. Hah. At this rate I might end up being the most handsome man alive. Hehe.\"","He stood there admiring his reflection for a full ten minutes before he finally left the room.","---","The academy campus was calm in the evening light. A cool breeze moved through the open walkways, touching his skin as he strolled without any particular destination in mind. The sky had turned a soft orange at the edges.","He walked slowly, hands in his pockets.","’Today is Thursday,’ he thought. ’Next Saturday is the first unit test. A VR battle. Our class against Class B-2.’","He wasn’t worried about the result. His class was strong. Strong enough that a loss would genuinely be surprising.","But then his expression became more focused.","’What I’m curious about is the point system. How do individual points work inside a team battle format?’","That was the part he actually wanted to understand before the day arrived."]},{"number":74,"title":"Chapter 74: New Friend","paragraphs":["He kept walking, turning it over quietly in his mind as the evening settled across the campus around him.","Noah entered the shopping area on campus.","This was the same place where the incident had occurred roughly a week and a half ago. The attack had left a good portion of it destroyed.","But somehow, in just a few days, everything had been rebuilt and reopened as if nothing had happened at all.","Students had returned without much hesitation, filling the walkways and shops the same way they always had.","Noah slowed as he approached a familiar building.","The café. The same one he had been standing near when the attack broke out.","He looked at it for a moment. \"Hah.\" He let out a quiet breath. \"Well. It’s alright now.\"","He stepped forward, and the glass door slid open automatically, sensing him as he approached.","Inside, the café was warm and smelled of coffee and baked goods. Most of the tables were taken. First-year and second-year students filled the space, talking in small groups or sitting quietly over their drinks. The low hum of conversation filled the room.","Noah scanned the tables for somewhere to sit.","Then he stopped.","At a table near the side wall sat a young woman he recognized. She was alone, working through a pastry with quiet concentration. Her black hair was short, cut neatly. She wore round black-rimmed glasses, a grey t-shirt tucked into a black flowing skirt that fell just below her knees.","It was Mary.","Noah smiled to himself and walked over.","\"Hey, Mary.\" He stopped beside her table.","\"How have you been? I haven’t spoken to you in a while. Mind if I sit?\"","His tone was easy and friendly.","Mary, who had been happily focused on her pastry, flinched at the sound of her name.","\"Wh-who?\" She looked up.","Her dark eyes went wide behind her glasses. \"N–Noah! Why are you here? And why do you want to sit with me?\"","Noah’s lips twitched slightly at her flustered reaction.","He kept his expression gentle and pulled out the chair across from her, sitting down without making a big deal of it.","\"Why would I be here? For coffee, obviously.\" He set his elbows on the table lightly. \"And I spotted you when I came in. We know each other, so I came to say hello. Is that strange?\"","Mary blinked. Then she straightened up and gave a small nod, looking briefly embarrassed.","\"Right. Of course. Everyone comes here for coffee. That was a silly thing for me to ask. Sorry.\" She let out a short breath and smiled.","A staff member came over to take his order. Noah asked for a cappuccino, and the staff member moved off. He turned back to Mary.","\"So how are you doing? Settling in alright? Enjoying the academy so far?\"","Mary considered the question for a moment, turning her fork idly against her plate.","\"It’s good, I think. The academy itself is fine.\" She paused. \"Though the incident was a terrible thing. Really dangerous and sad.\" She looked at him for a brief moment before continuing.","\"I wasn’t involved in it directly, so I can’t really say what it was like for the people who were. You and the others who were actually there...\" She trailed off slightly. \"You’re the ones who know what it was really like. I’m just glad you came out of it okay.\"","Noah leaned back in his chair.","\"It was dangerous,\" he said simply. \"And frightening, honestly. But a lot of people made it through. And in the end, this is exactly the kind of situation we came here to learn how to face.\"","Mary nodded slowly, her voice quieter now. \"That’s true.\"","Noah watched her for a moment. She had gone back to her pastry, picking at it gently, her expression soft and a little thoughtful.","He smiled to himself.","’She’s not like the main heroines in the stories. Not the kind of striking beauty that takes everyone’s attention.’ He rested his chin on his hand.","’But Mary is genuinely cute in her own way. I won’t pretend otherwise. If I ever thought about having a girlfriend, I think I’d want someone like her.’","No matter how much danger was ahead of him in the future, Noah was still a young man at an age where they were naturally curious about love and dating.","In his last life, he never tried dating someone because of studies and his future, while using his free time on playing games and other things. So dating was out of the question.","But that didn’t mean he was not interested.","Now he was in another world as a handsome young man. But once again, he needed to work hard to survive in this world.","Whenever he watched those beautiful female leads of the game, sometimes a thought always came to him. What if he could get them as his lovers, just like how it happens in novels?","But he also didn’t want to have main heroines as a girlfriend. Being a game where there was a harem in it, that simply meant there would be a lot of dangerous events related to the heroines. Where Damien would help them, save them, and through that get closer.","If he meddled and tried to get one of them, that meant he would have to face those events.","So if he ever wanted to have a girlfriend, he would choose someone like Mary. An extra who was not extremely beautiful, but still attractive. At least in Noah’s eyes.","While Noah was lost in his thoughts—","His cappuccino arrived at the table.","He wrapped both hands around the warm cup and took a slow sip.","\"By the way, Mary.\" He looked at her. \"I’ve noticed for a while... you are always alone. Don’t you have any friends?\"","Mary, who had once again been focused on enjoying her sweet, stiffened.","Then, looking at Noah with a forced smile, she replied, \"Wh-what do you mean I don’t have friends? I do have... just very few... who are very busy.\"","Noah caught her forced expression.","He put the cup of coffee on the table and said with a smile, \"Then add me to your small friend list.. let me be your new friend.\""]},{"number":75,"title":"Chapter 75: Getting Closer?","paragraphs":["Mary set her fork down and looked at him with wide eyes. \"Wait. You want to become friends with me?\"","\"Yeah,\" Noah said simply. \"I do.\"","She stared at him for a moment as if waiting for a punchline that wasn’t coming.","\"But... why?\" Her voice dropped slightly. \"I mean, you’re from a noble family. You’re...\" She glanced at him briefly, then looked away.","\"You’re obviously very good looking. And you already seem to get along well with Lyria and Damien and the others. So why would you want to be friends with someone like me?\" She folded her hands in her lap. \"I’m just... ordinary. A commoner. Not even talented the way Arisha is.\"","Noah went quiet for a moment. He hadn’t expected that.","*Was she always this conscious of where she stood?*","He looked at her properly. She wasn’t putting on false modesty. She genuinely meant every word of it. That was what caught him off guard.","He leaned forward slightly and gave her the warmest smile he could manage.","\"How can you think that way?\" His tone was easy.","\"Why would my background or my face have anything to do with whether I want to be your friend? Those things don’t matter for that.\" He paused, then added, \"And for the record, you’re cute. So stop selling yourself short on that front too. As for me being noble... I’m exiled, so I’m no better than a commoner. As for talent...\" he laughed softly, \"I’d bet you have more of it than me. Haha.\"","Mary’s cheeks flushed a light pink at the word cute. She dropped her gaze to the table.","\"Y-you think so?\" she said quietly. \"Thank you.\"","\"I mean it.\" He settled back in his chair. \"So, we are friends from now on. And if you ever have a problem or need help with something, just say the word.\"","Mary looked at him from across the table. The Noah sitting in front of her was nothing like the version she had heard about in rumors around campus.","She wasn’t entirely sure what she had expected, but it wasn’t this. This easy, warm, completely kind person who had just sat himself down across from her and meant every word he said.","She felt her shoulders relax without knowing. \"Okay, Noah.\"","He smiled and reached into his storage ring, pulling out his phone and setting it on the table between them.","\"Then you’ll have to give me your number.\"","She pulled out her own phone. \"Yes, alright.\"","They exchanged contacts without any fuss, and Noah slipped his phone back into his ring.","\"One more thing.\" He rested his arms on the table. \"I’m planning to focus on training until the VR battle next week. But after that, on the weekend. If you’re free, how about we go into Novaris City and hang out for a bit?\"","Mary looked up from her phone.","\"You... want to take me out on the weekend?\" She processed the words for a second. \"Like... taking me on a date?\"","Her hand moved to cover her mouth as her cheeks went noticeably pink.","Noah rested his right elbow on the table and propped his chin up on his palm. His left hand moved idly, his index finger tracing slow circles around the rim of his coffee cup.","\"Date is a bit of a misleading word when I’m asking as a friend,\" he said, his tone teasing. \"I just meant hanging out together. But...\" The corner of his mouth curved slightly. \"If you want it to be a date, I genuinely don’t mind. I can make it feel like one.\"","\"Ehh!\" Mary straightened up immediately, shaking her head. \"That’s not what I meant! I just, yes, I can go, but...\" She fumbled slightly over her words. \"Going out with just one person. A man. I haven’t really done that before.\"","\"Then it’ll be fun,\" Noah said, completely unbothered. \"You don’t need to overthink it. We’ll just enjoy ourselves.\"","Mary looked at him. His expression was open and genuine, no pressure behind it, just a kind of sincerity that was somehow harder to refuse.","She gave a small nod.","\"Okay. I’ll come.\"","Noah’s smile widened. \"Hehe. Thanks. I’ll look forward to it.\"","---","They left the café together a little while later, stepping out into the evening air side by side.","The sky above the campus had deepened into a soft dark blue, the last of the daylight fading at the edges. A cool breeze moved between the buildings, quiet and unhurried.","Neither of them said anything for a moment.","It was a comfortable kind of silence.","\"By the way... after that day in the cafeteria. Has Edward ever bothered you?\" he asked, looking straight ahead.","He was curious about this. That day the drama had occurred because Mary, as a commoner, had collided with an arrogant young master who was then beaten by Noah. But surprisingly, he hadn’t heard a single word about Edward doing anything to Mary since then.","\"No... surprisingly he never tried anything.\" She replied, thinking back to the incident that had happened with her.","\"That’s good news then. Seems like he became a better student.\"","\"Really? You really think so?\" she asked, looking at him. Her eyes were gazing at him through her glasses.","\"There’s a possibility. I mean, I was a bad boy as well. But then I changed, didn’t I?\"","\"That’s true.\" Mary nodded with understanding.","\"Oh, so you actually used to think I was a bad guy?\" Noah turned to her with a slight frown. His expression was displeased.","Which made Mary nervous and flustered. \"No! No! I didn’t mean it that way! I mean yes, I used to think you weren’t a good guy– No wait, I mean, oh... shit!\"","\"Pff — hahaha!\" Noah burst into laughter seeing her expression.","She blinked at him in confusion about why he was laughing like that.","Then the realization hit her. He had been teasing her.","She turned to face him and pointed her finger at him, her cheeks pink. \"You! You- you were making fun of me! Don’t talk to me. Hmph!\" She turned away with an annoyed pout.","\"Okay, okay. I’m sorry alright. I won’t do it again.\"","\"I said don’t talk to me.\"","Noah suddenly stopped and went completely silent. His expression turned cold.","Not hearing anything from him, she turned to look at his face.","\"I said I was sorry, didn’t I? Then why are you acting so arrogant?\" He said in cold tone.","With no warmth in it.","\"Heeeh!\" A small startled sound left her mouth after hearing his cold words and seeing his stern expression."]}]);
